	print nohdr************************************************************************************************                                                                                             **	DOS 3.3 File System Translator for GS/OS                                              **                                                                                             **	Copyright Apple Computer Inc. 1988-1992  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED                          **                                                                                             **                                                                                             *******************************************************************************************************	REVISION HISTORY:	*****************************************************************	August 15, 1988	Monte Benaresh**		Created this file and entered basic directives, includes, etc.*		At this point the preliminary ERS, version 0.1, is about to be*		released.**		Much of this file is based on the source for the ProDOS FST by*		Rob Turner.**	October 27, 1988 Monte Benaresh**		All the code needed for the OPEN call is essentially completed.*		Ported dispatch "shell" routines from the ProDOS FST v02.00.*		Existing source assembles, and code is about to be set up*		for testing under the GS/OS exerciser.**	November 17, 1988 Monte Benaresh**		The OPEN, VOLUME, and GET_FILE_INFO calls are now functional and*		the Finder will mount DOS 3.3 disks.**	August 13, 1989 Monte Benaresh**		All calls are now implemented, and the FST is just a few hours away*		from being called Alpha.**	August 14, 1989 Monte Benaresh**		Projectorized the source and created a makefile.** 1.0 d17* 10/08/90	CAF	Changed the code in match_vcr to increment the vcr open count before*			trying to read in some blocks from the disk.  I did this because SCM*			was throwing out the VCR when it got the disk_switched error from the*			appledisk5.25, so an FCR would be created with a link to no VCR - when*			you tried to close the FCR, SCM would die.  Fixed following bugs:*				EDS213WMP - changed flush to check for pcount max = 2.*				EDS212WMP - changed parameter table to not include pcount as a parm.*				EDS205WMP - uncommented some existing code which fixed it.*				EDS207WMP - added a check for the resource_num parameter.*				EDS208WMP - fixed by match_vcr addition.*				EDS209WMP - fixed by EDS207WMP fix.*				EDS210WMP - changed code in open to preserve error number.*				EDS211WMP - fixed by commenting out code which copied old fcr*					    into new fcr in open call.*				EDS222WMP - changed gfi to put total_blocks into aux_type for c0.** 1.0 d18* 10/15/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				EDS224WMP - Changed read code to skip the high bit stripping for dirs.* 10/17/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				APG209WMP - Volume call was getting a $2C error because of a request*					    count to the driver of $100, I changed this to a bouncing*					    error.*				EDS226WMP - Same fix as APG209WMP*				EDS215WMP - The newline code for a single char was transferring the*					    data backwards, so I changed the loop to go forwards.  Also*					    the local transfer count was not being returned correctly.*				EDS214WMP - The local transfer count in newline was not being returned*					    correctly (it was being returned as 0), so the fst would*					    sit and spin forever because the request_count was never met.** 1.0 d19 - Beta Candidate* 11/02/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				LYP225LWA - Changed volume size constants used in volume_s to correct values.*				LYP226LWA - Changed class 0 version of volume_s to not divide free block*					    count by 2.*				LYP227LWA - Changed parse_path to check for a class 0 separator as well*					    as a class 1 separator at the start of the pathname.*				LYP229LWA - Changed class 0 getfileinfo to check to see if the file is a directory*					    before stuffing the total_blocks into the aux_type.** 1.0 d20 - Beta Candidate* 11/06/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				LYP227LWA - removed addition to parse_path added on 11/02/90, and changed*					    get_dev_num_s to check for a duplicate volume error and mask it*					    into a volume not found error.*				LYP230LWA - changed open to zero out the resource_blocks field.** 1.0 d21 - Beta Candidate* 11/06/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				LYP231LWA - changed open_setup to check to see if a volume is a dos*					    volume and that it is online before trying to create a vcr*					    for it.*				LYP228LWA - same as 231.*			Completely rewrote most of open_setup because the algorithm used in finding*			volumes and building vcr's was not handling the operation correctly.*			Fixed a bug in find_vol_online where it was not returning a vol_not_found*			error and so the call would not bounce to other fsts.*			Fixed get_dir_entry to update the vcr_dev if the disk moves.*			Fixed a bug in get_dir_entry where the drvr_dev_num was not being setup if the end_of_dir*			had been reached, so a subsequent get_last_dev call would not work correctly.*				* 1.0 d22 - Beta Candidate* 11/09/90	CAF	Fixed a bug in parse_path where it was executing 16 bit code in 8 bit mode.*			Fixed a bug in open_setup where I was not setting up a pointer before a call, and*			so the fst was getting confused enough to cause SCM to commit hari-kari.*				LYP237LWA - Fixed a bug in open_setup that was causing vcrs to be dumped.** 1.0 d23* 11/28/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				LYP243LWA - changed newline code to strip the high bits off of text*					    file data during xfer.*				LYP248LWA - changed some 8/16bit A errors in newline read.*				LYP247LWA - same as LYP248LWA*				LYP245LWA - same as LYP248LWA*				LYP246LWA - same as LYP248LWA*				LYP238LWA - changed pblock copy data to null out the blocks_used field.*				LYP241LWA - changed get_dir_entry to check for out of range values*					    when base = 2.** 1.0 d24* 12/06/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				LYP249LWA - Fixed a bug in read where it wasn't taking into account*					    the data_offset into a file.*				LYP252LWA - same as 249.*				LYP250LWA - Fixed a bug in newline_read where it wasn't using*					    long index registers during the newline compare, and*					    so any multiple of $100 would give a length of $00.*			Fixed a bug where newline mode with > 1 char would not work on text files.** 1.0 d25* 12/07/90	CAF	Changed volume_s to output the volume name on a dup_vol error.** 1.0 d26* 12/18/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				LYP254LWA - changed open to not output blocks_used parameter.*				LYP255LWA - changed allocate_vcr to allow the starting search*					    device (supposed_dev) to be setup by the caller.** 1.0 d27* 12/19/90	CAF	Fixed Bugs:*				LYP256LWA - changed open to special case the directory file.*				LYP257LWA - changed gfi to special case a class 1 call on a directory.*				LYP258LWA - changed not_supported2 and not_supported to return drvr_wr_prot.*				LYP259LWA - changed not_supported2 and not_supported to return drvr_wr_prot.*				LYP260LWA - changed not_supported2 and not_supported to return drvr_wr_prot.*				LYP261LWA - changed not_supported2 and not_supported to return drvr_wr_prot.*				LYP262LWA - changed not_supported2 and not_supported to return drvr_wr_prot.*				LYP263LWA - changed not_supported2 and not_supported to return drvr_wr_prot.** 1.0 b01* 12/19/90	CAF/JEV	Fixed a bug that was causing a vcr to be thrown out during a gfi call.*			Added "support" for judge_name call ($07).** 1.0 b02	jev	Changed how volume names are generated.  It was felt that just 'DOS 3.3 Vxxxx' was*			all that was needed.** 1.0 b03	jev	Fixed Bug:*				BGK053LWA - changed error code from a $60 to $4A* 3/31/91	jev	changed vol_not_found error to unknown vol error if we try to access any*			other device other than an 5.25.* 3/31/91	jev	fixed problem with checking for correct pcount.* 3/31/91	jev	added error priority support.  Added new flags in FST header*			to indicate apple format and read-only fst.* 8/18/91	jev	Fixed Bug:*				86672 - add check in parsepath to check for path2 to see if*				it exsists or is too long even though we don't use it *				because we con't do a changepath.  But we need to be a *				good FST and return $40 instead of a $45 if the path is bad.* 8/19/91	jev	Fixed Do_Option_list.  Was not setting up the length of the data.* 8/21/91	jev	Changed max-pcnt for Judename call to 6.  Fixes a bug reported by *			developer in which DOS3.3 returns a bad pcount error instead of an*			invalidFSTop for a judeName call.** 9/18/91	jev	fixed open call to resource fork.  Any open call to a resource fork*			passed to this fst would return res_not_found error even the destination*			volume was not a DOS 3.3 volume.  Moved this check to after the destination*			was located because this is a non-bouncing error and we don't want to return*			this error unless the destination belongs to us.** 9/19/91	jev	Fixed Bug:*				86425 - open call with invalid access to any target would return*				invalid access even if the target was not a DOS 3.3 file.*				Moved access check to after the destination was located as above.** 11/19/91	GAB	Fixed occurances of returning VolumeNotFound errors when that*			particular error shouldn't be returned.  (Confuses SCM's error*			priority logic.)**			Changed device_id routine so that it no longer performs a Status*			call to the device driver simply to have the dispatcher set the*			DIB pointer on direct page.  The dispatcher has a call that will*			perform this service without getting the driver involved.** 12/05/91	GAB	Change maximum allowable pCount for ChangePath call to 3.** 01/08/92	GAB	Fixed READ call to properly initialize fde_ptr before it tries*			to use it.  It was using an invalid pointer when it tried to*			retrieve the first track/sector list location out of the*			directory entry.**			Fixed READ call to decrement the destination pointer after*			moving an odd number of bytes out of the sector buffer.  When*			moving an odd number of bytes, it moved the first byte, then*			incremented the destination pointer and performed the remainder*			of the move 2 bytes at a time.  Once it had moved the remainder*			of the sector buffer to the caller's buffer, it was adjusting*			the destination pointer by the number of bytes moved (which*			skipped one byte, due to the initial increment).  It was then*			going back to read the next sector to finish the call, but*			using the invalid (off-by-one) destination pointer.**			Changed 'brl' instructions to 'bra' wherever possible** 02/07/92	MSD	Changed version number to 01.00 (final).** 02/19/92 - Monte Benaresh*			Added code to the OPEN call to zero-out the resource_eof field*			when the param is active, and changed to param copy tables for*			GET_DIR_ENTRY and GET_FILE_INFO to zero out the resource_eof*			and resource_blocks fields when those params are active.** 19-Feb-92 Dave Lyons*			Rolled version to $0101 and v01.01 for Monte's change.** 02/20/92 - Monte Benaresh*			Fixed problem in find_eof with 0-length text files.*			Bumped version to 1.02.************************************************************************************************** BEGIN 6.0.1** 26-May-92 Dave Lyons for 6.0.1** Try changing name to "Apple II DOS 3.3" instead of just "DOS 3.3", to avoid* confusion with MS-DOS.** 7-Nov-92 DAL with jcm, version 1.3d12** Added an entry to the end of fcr_to_pblk so that Open will stop when pcount is 15 instead* of trashing a variable amount of memory past the end of the parameter block.*** 2-Apr-93 SS -- Changed version to $0103 for 6.0.1 (final)** 5-May-93 DAL -- for 6.0.1d17** Handle zero-length filenames like deleted directory entries, because the Finder* gets really confused on a zero-length name, and it doesn't make much sense to* begin with.  Some DOS 3.3 disks have zero-length filenames to make the catalog* look pretty.************************************************************************************************	machine M65816	string asis	print off		include 'my.all.macros'	include 'm16.debug'	;load 'C.Floor:MPW:aiigsincludes:my.cmn.d'	include 'my.common.equ'	include 'param.records'	include 'DOS.FST.identifiers'	print on;======================================================================;Below is the FST header definition used by GS/OS at boot time;;This PROC was adapted directly from the ProDOS FST v02.00 by Rob Turner;;======================================================================				EXPORT	fst_header	fst_header	PROC		import appl_call		import system_call		EXPORT	code_startcode_start            		DC.B	'FST '		;Says I'm an FST		DC.L	appl_call	;Process a normal application call		DC.L	system_call	;Process an FST system call		DC.W	my_id		;ID number (DOS 3.3) = $02		DC.W	$1803		;don't uppercase pathnames, not formattable, strip high bit(?).					;read-only,apple II format		DC.W	$0103		;Version 1.03 final		DC.W	256		;block size		DC.L	560		;Max Blocks (140K)		DC.L	32		;Min Blocks-need at least 2 tracks.		DC.L	$FFFFFFFF	;max file size in bytes.		DC.L	$0000		;reserved		DC.B	@n_end-@n_strt	;length of next field@n_strt		DC.B	'Apple II DOS 3.3'	@n_end		dc.b	@c_end-@c_strt	;length of comment@c_strt		DC.B	'DOS 3.3 FST           v01.03'					;comment field@c_end		DC.W	0000		;reserved field		dc.b	'DOS 3.3 FST. Written by Monte Benaresh, maintained by Cary '		dc.b	'Farrier and Jack Valois.  Tested by Linda Pan.  '		dc.b	'Copyright 1992 Apple Computer'		ENDP		print off	include 'DOS.FST.storage'		print onopen_s		PROCNAME		;shell for open call		import open		stz error		jsl lock_mem		;	No need to check for the p_count here anymore.  It is all done;	at the app entry point now.;;check_pcount;		lda class		;get the class of the call;		beq @class0		;if class 0, no pcount;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #open1.pmax;		bcc @class0;		lda #invalid_pcount	;too big;		sta error;		bra exit;@ok; moved these checks into open call.  we need to check to see if this; is a DOS3.3 volume first before we return a non-bouncing error; 							9/17/91	JEV;@check_access;		cmp #4			;enough parameters for request_access?;		bcc @class0		;no, can't check it		;		ldy #open1.request_access;		lda [param_blk_ptr],y	;get the request access word;		and #%0000000000000010	;check for write access;		beq @ok0		;no write access		;		lda #invalid_access;		sta  error;		bra exit;@ok0					; opening resource fork?;		bra @class0;;		lda  p_cnt;		cmp  #5;		bcc  @class0		; pcount too small ->		;		ldy  #open1.resource_number;		lda  [<param_blk_ptr],y;		beq  @class0		; ok ->		;		cmp  #1			; == 1?;		beq  @class0		; ok ->;		bne  @range_err		; no ->		;;		lda  #res_not_found;		sta  error;		bra  exit;@range_err	lda  #parm_range_err;		sta  error;		bra  exit		@class0		jsr open		sta error		;save error		lda gen_buf_vp		tax		ora gen_buf_vp+2		beq @skip3		ldy gen_buf_vp+2		jsl release_seg@skip3exit		;brk $22		jsl unlock_mem		lda error		;restore error		cmp #1			;set carry accordingly		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		;brk $11		jml sys_exiterror		ds.w 1			;temp storage for error code		ENDPvolume_s	PROC			;shell for volume call		import volume		import free_sectors		import load_cat_secs		import match_vcr		import allocate_vcr		import device_id		;stz gen_buf_vp		;this is now done on entry		;stz gen_buf_vp+2		stz vcr_fcr_flags	;init flags		;brk $13		jsl lock_mem		jsr device_id		; we're looking for a device_id of $00		bcs err_done		beq @device_ok		lda #unknown_vol	; not a 5.25' drive return a bouncing error		bra err_done@device_ok		lda class		beq @class0@class1;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #volume1.pmax;		bcc @ok1;		lda #invalid_pcount;		brl exit@ok1		ldy #volume1.vol_name	;copy pointer to direct page		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2		lda #vol_max_char+4	;check the buffer size		cmp [user_ptr]		bcc @ok2		lda #vol_max_char+1	;this is the size we need		ldy #$0002		;point to string length field		sta [user_ptr],y	;let caller know what we need		lda #buff_too_small		;pha		;php		brl exit@ok2		bra get_buffs@class0		ldy #volume0.vol_name	;copy pointer to direct page		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2get_buffs		lda #vol_name_buf		;get address of this internal buffer		sta <vol_name_ptr		lda #gen_buf_size	;let's get some buffer space for the vtoc & directory		jsl alloc_seg		bcc @ok		lda #out_of_mem		;can't get buffer space		brl done@ok		stx gen_buf_vp		;4K buffer used by volume routine		sty gen_buf_vp+2		jsl deref		stx <gen_buf_ptr		sty <gen_buf_ptr+2		;lda gbuf_ptr		;sta <gen_buf_ptr		;lda gbuf_ptr+2		;sta <gen_buf_ptr+2		;brk $A9		jsr volume		bcc ok1@vol_error				;volume identification failed		cmp #drvr_bad_parm	; bad parameter?		beq @mask		; yes ->		cmp #drvr_bad_count	; bad count because of the $100 request count?		bne err_done		; no, return the error back up ->@mask		lda #unknown_vol	;translate to bouncing errorerr_done	sec		brl done		;if error, pack up and leaveok1		lda #<vol_name_buf		;set up our volume name for other routines		sta <volname_buf_ptr		lda #^vol_name_buf		sta <volname_buf_ptr+2				lda  drvr_dev_num	; look in this device		sta  supposed_dev		jsr allocate_vcr		bcc  have_vcr				cmp  #dup_volume	; duplicate volume error ?		bne  err_done		; no ->				lda  path_flag		; device name only?		and  #$4000		beq  name_out		; yes ->		err_bra		lda  #dup_volume	; no ->		bra  err_done		** copy the volume name to the output buffer anyways*name_out	lda class		;output the volume name		beq @class0@class1		lda (vol_name_ptr)	;get volume name length		inc a			;account for leading character		ldy #2			;point to start of g-string		sta [user_ptr],y	;set the length		lda <user_ptr		clc		adc #$0003		;bump pointer to look at g-string plus room for…					;…leading '/' or ':'		sta <user_ptr		bcc @no_carry		inc <user_ptr+2@no_carry		ldy #$0002		;point to 1st char		bra @copy_string		;we're now ready to copy@class0				lda (vol_name_ptr)	;get length		inc a			;account for leading character		sta [user_ptr]@copy_string		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF		ldy #$0002@loop		lda (vol_name_ptr),y		beq @done		;if we hit a null, that's the end of the volume name		sta [user_ptr],y		iny		bpl @loop		;use bpl so if something weird happens, the most we'll…					;…trash is 32K!@done		rep #%00100000		LONGA ON		lda class		bne @sep1@sep0		ldy #1			;point to space for '/'		lda [user_ptr],y		and #$FF00		;erase the garbage		ora #'/'		;place the slash		sta [user_ptr],y				bra  err_bra		; up ->		@sep1		ldy #1			;point to space for ':'		lda [user_ptr],y		and #$FF00		;erase the garbage		ora #':'		;place the colon		sta [user_ptr],y				bra  err_bra		; up ->		****************		have_vcr		lda class		;here we go again!		beq @class0@class1		lda (vol_name_ptr)	;get volume name length		inc a			;account for leading character		ldy #2			;point to start of g-string		sta [user_ptr],y	;set the length		lda <user_ptr		clc		adc #$0003		;bump pointer to look at g-string plus room for…					;…leading '/' or ':'		sta <user_ptr		bcc @no_carry		inc <user_ptr+2@no_carry		ldy #$0002		;point to 1st char		bra copy_string		;we're now ready to copy@class0				lda (vol_name_ptr)	;get length		inc a			;account for leading character		sta [user_ptr]copy_string		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF		ldy #$0002@loop		lda (vol_name_ptr),y		beq @done		;if we hit a null, that's the end of the volume name		sta [user_ptr],y		iny		bpl @loop		;use bpl so if something weird happens, the most we'll…					;…trash is 32K!@done		rep #%00100000		LONGA ON** output the total_blocks and free_blocks*		lda class		bne @class1@class0		ldy #1			;point to space for '/'		lda [user_ptr],y		and #$FF00		;erase the garbage		ora #'/'		;place the slash		sta [user_ptr],y		ldy #vtoc_sectors	;get # of sector per track		lda [vol_buf_ptr],y		and #32		bne @32a		;there are 32 sectors per track		lda #$230		;# of 512-byte blocks on 5 1/4 volume		bra @stor@32a		lda #$640		;# of 512-byte blocks on a 3 1/2@stor		ldy #volume0.total_blocks		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		lda #$0000		sta [param_blk_ptr],y	;zero the high word		jsr free_sectors		ldy #volume0.free_blocks		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		lda #$0000		sta [param_blk_ptr],y	;zero the high word		lda #my_id		;FST ID		ldy #volume0.file_sys_id		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		clc			;call successful		bra done@class1		ldy #1			;point to space for ':'		lda [user_ptr],y		and #$FF00		;erase the garbage		ora #':'		;place the colon		sta [user_ptr],y		lda p_cnt		sta param_countdn		dec param_countdn	;this way we can use bmi		dec param_countdn	;dev_name		dec param_countdn	;vol_name		bmi done				;now we want total_blocks		ldy #vtoc_sectors	;get # of sector per track		lda [vol_buf_ptr],y		and #32		bne @32			;there are 32 sectors per track		lda #$230		;# of sectors on 5 1/4 volume		bra @store@32		lda #$640		;# of sectors on a 3 1/2@store		ldy #volume1.total_blocks		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		lda #$0000		sta [param_blk_ptr],y	;zero the high word		dec param_countdn		bmi done				;get blocks free		jsr free_sectors		ldy #volume1.free_blocks		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		lda #$0000		sta [param_blk_ptr],y	;zero the high word		dec param_countdn		bmi done		lda #my_id		;FST ID		ldy #volume1.file_sys_id		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		dec param_countdn		bmi done		lda #$0100		;this is our "block" size		ldy #volume1.block_size		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		clc			;call successful		lda #0exitdone		pha		php		;jsl unlock_mem		bcc @no_error		;if no error, let VCR's stay		bit vcr_fcr_flags	;check whether we alocated a VCR		bpl @no_vcr		;high bit tells whether VCR was allocated@cancel_vcr		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		lda #$0000		sta [vcr_ptr],y		;must zero the open count to release it!		ldy #vcr_id		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;get ID of the VCR		jsl release_vcr		;this invokes sys_remove_vol call to this fst@no_vcr@no_error		lda gen_buf_vp		;we may have to release this segment		tax		ora gen_buf_vp+2		beq @skip3		ldy gen_buf_vp+2		jsl release_seg@skip3		plp		pla		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		;brk $88		jml sys_exitparam_countdn	ds.w 1			;local countdown var		ENDPfree_sectors	PROC		;determine the number of free sectors listed in the vtoc				;vtoc must be at vol_buf_ptr				;result is in accumulator		;first set up some looping limits		ldy #vtoc_sectors	;number of sectors per track		lda [vol_buf_ptr],y		and #$00FF		;take low byte		lsr a		lsr a		lsr a		lsr a			;divide by 16 to get # of words of bitmap per track		sta words		stz result		;start with a clean slate				;let the loops begin!		ldy #vtoc_tracks	;# of tracks on the disk		lda [vol_buf_ptr],y		and #$00FF		sta track_index@track_loop		lda words		sta words_index		lda track_index		dec a		bmi done		sta track_index		asl a		asl a			;multiply by 4 to get byte offset. this should clear carry		adc #vtoc_bitmap	;add offset to start of bitmap. carry should be clear		tay@word_loop	lda [vol_buf_ptr],y	;get a bitmap word		sta bitmap_temp		lda result		ldx #$0010@bit_loop	asl bitmap_temp		adc #$0000		;carry set if we just shifted a high bit		dex		bne @bit_loop		sta result		dec words_index		beq @track_loop		iny		iny			;bump index to next word		bra @word_loopdone		lda result		;this is a good place for the result		rtswords		ds 1result		ds 1track_index	ds 1words_index	ds 1bitmap_temp	ds 1		ENDPget_file_info_s	PROC			;shell for get_file_info call		import open_setup		import match_vcr		import load_cat_secs		import search_fcr		import check_dir		import get_file_info		import fill_param		import get_file_info0_f		import get_file_info1_f		import do_option_list		stz temp_vp		stz temp_vp+2		;brk $AC		jsl lock_mem;		lda class;		beq @class0;@class1;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #get_file_info1.pmax;		bcc @ok;		lda #invalid_pcount;		brl error;@ok;		bra do_it;@class0do_it		jsr open_setup		;among other things, this will find VCR for…					;…this volume name and verify identity		bcc @ok1		brl pack_up@ok1		;jsr match_vcr		;find VCR for this volume name and verify identity		;bcc @ok2		;brl pack_up		;return with duplicate volume error@ok2		;beq no_vcrfound_vcr			;we found the volume's vcr		stz good_vcr		;flag to say we have a vcr		ldy #vcr_buf_vp		lda [vcr_ptr],y		tax		iny		iny		lda [vcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		;stx gen_buf_ptr		;sty gen_buf_ptr+2	;set up correct buffer for check_dir		stx vol_buf_ptr		sty vol_buf_ptr+2	;set up correct buffer for check_dir		ldy #vcr_cat_sec_count		lda [vcr_ptr],y		sta cat_sec_count	;get that right, too		;bra have_vcrno_vcr		;lda #$8000		;sta good_vcr		;keep flag to tell whether we have a vcr		;jsr load_cat_secs		;bcc check_file		;brl pack_up@ok3have_vcrcheck_file			;was there a file to get info on?		lda (file_name_ptr)	;was there a filename?		bne handle_filehandle_vol					;a bunch of things get zeroes		stz aux_type		;fill the globals		stz eof+2		stz  blks_used				lda cat_sec_count		inc  a			;account for vtoc		ldx  class		bne  @1		sta blks_used@1		xba		sta eof		lda #$000F		sta os_type		sta stor_type		lda #access_unlocked		sta access		bra stuff_globalshandle_file		;brk $02		;lda good_vcr		;did we have a valid vcr?		;bne chk_dir		;no, check the directory		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;see if any files are already open in this vcr		beq chk_dir		;we'll have to look in the directory		jsr search_fcr		;this routine will return number of fcr, for previous…					;…open of the file named in file_name_ptr, in old_fcr		;bcs chk_dir		;not found, check directory		bcc from_fcr		;fetch all info from fcr		chk_dir				;does this guy exist in the directory?		jsr check_dir		;this sub checks for filename in file_name_ptr		bcc @ok		lda #dir_error		;problem with the directory structure		brl pack_up@ok		lda fde_index		bpl filename_goodfile_not_here		;file not on this volume		lda #file_not_found		brl pack_upfilename_good			;file exists in directorygo_to_disk				;otherwise, we have to get it ourselves from disk		;lda #file_buf_size	;request segments for file buffers  ***************		;jsl alloc_seg		;bcc @ok1		;lda #out_of_mem		;we *must* have those buffers!		;bra error;@ok1		;stx temp_vp		;sty temp_vp+2		;jsl deref		;stx <fcr_buf_ptr		;sty <fcr_buf_ptr+2					;make it look like we have an FCR					;hopefully, the device number will be left over from					;the "volume" routine		lda gbuf_ptr		;use system gbuf		sta <fcr_buf_ptr		lda gbuf_ptr+2		sta <fcr_buf_ptr+2		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		jsr get_file_info	;get all the good stuff		bcc @ok2		bra error		;return with driver error@ok2stuff_globals				;now copy from globals to user param list		lda class		bne class1class0		lda #$0001		sta p_cnt		;this will make the fill_param tables work right						lda  os_type		cmp  #$0F		bne  @cont		lda  #$230		; auxtype = total blocks		sta  aux_type		@cont		lda #<get_file_info0_f		sta <fill_tabl		;set up for right parameter fill table		jsr fill_param		lda #0		bra pack_up		;all done!class1		lda #<get_file_info1_f		sta <fill_tabl		;set up for right parameter fill table		jsr fill_param		lda p_cnt		cmp #8			;do we need option list?		bcc @no_list		ldy #get_file_info1.option_list		jsr do_option_list		bcc @done		lda #buff_too_small		bra pack_up@no_list@done		lda #0		bra pack_upfrom_fcr			;pull info out of the fcr and into the globals		ldy #fcr_access		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		sta access		ldy #fcr_eof		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		sta eof		iny		iny		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		sta eof+2		ldy #fcr_aux		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		sta aux_type		ldy #fcr_type		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		sta os_type		ldy #fcr_blks_used		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		sta blks_used		bra stuff_globals		;now give it all to the usererror		secpack_up		pha		;lda temp_vp		;tax		;ora temp_vp+2		;beq @skip1		;ldy temp_vp+2		;jsl release_seg@skip1		lda gen_buf_vp		tax		ora gen_buf_vp+2		beq @skip3		ldy gen_buf_vp+2		jsl release_seg@skip3exit		;brk $22		jsl unlock_mem		pla		cmp #1		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exitgood_vcr	ds 1		ENDPget_dir_entry_s	PROCNAME		;shell for the get_dir_entry call		import get_dir_entry		;brk $ED		jsl lock_mem		ldx <g_fcr_ptr		;SCM provides the FCR & VCR		ldy <g_fcr_ptr+2		jsl deref		stx <fcr_ptr		sty <fcr_ptr+2		ldx <g_vcr_ptr		ldy <g_vcr_ptr+2		jsl deref		stx <vcr_ptr		sty <vcr_ptr+2		lda #gen_buf_size	;let's get some buffer space for the vtoc & directory		jsl alloc_seg		bcc @mem_ok		lda #out_of_mem		;can't get buffer space		rts@mem_ok		stx gen_buf_vp		;4K buffer used by volume routine		sty gen_buf_vp+2		jsl deref		stx <gen_buf_ptr		sty <gen_buf_ptr+2		;lda #file_buf_size	;request segments for file buffers for find_eof		;jsl alloc_seg		;bcc @ok1		;lda #out_of_mem		;we *must* have those buffers!		;bra exit2@ok1		;stx temp_vp		;sty temp_vp+2		;jsl deref		;stx <fcr_buf_ptr		;sty <fcr_buf_ptr+2	;make it look like we have an FCR		lda gbuf_ptr		sta <fcr_buf_ptr	;use system gbuf		lda gbuf_ptr+2		sta <fcr_buf_ptr+2		lda class;		beq @class0;@class1;		WITH get_dir_entry1;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #pmax;		bcc @ok2;		lda #invalid_pcount;		sec;		bra exit;@ok2;		ENDWITH@class0		jsr get_dir_entryexit		;pha		;lda temp_vp		;tax		;ora temp_vp+2		;beq @skip1		;ldy temp_vp+2		;jsl release_seg@skip1		;plaexit2				;alternate exit which does not deallocate buffer		pha			;save error code		lda gen_buf_vp		tax		ora gen_buf_vp+2	;is vp valid?		beq @skip3		ldy gen_buf_vp+2		jsl release_seg@skip3		jsl unlock_mem		pla			;restore error		cmp #1		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDPread_s		PROCNAME		;shell for the read call		import read, find_fde		jsl lock_mem		ldx <g_fcr_ptr		;set up real pointers to vp's to fcr & vcr provided…		ldy <g_fcr_ptr+2	;…by the SCM		jsl deref		stx <fcr_ptr		sty <fcr_ptr+2		ldx <g_vcr_ptr		ldy <g_vcr_ptr+2		jsl deref		stx <vcr_ptr		sty <vcr_ptr+2; init fde_ptr properly so that if we need to read anything out of the file; directory entry, we won't be using an invalid pointer (and reading who-knows-what)		ldy  #vcr_buf_vp	;set up correct buffer for find_fde		lda  [vcr_ptr],y		tax		iny		iny		lda  [vcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl  deref		stx  vol_buf_ptr		sty  vol_buf_ptr+2		ldy #fcr_fde_num		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;need these to set up ptr to fde		tax		ldy #fcr_cat_sec		lda [fcr_ptr],y		jsr find_fde		;this sets up fde_ptr;		lda class;		beq @class0;@class1;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #read1.pmax;		bcc @ok1;		lda #invalid_pcount;		sec;		bra exit;@ok1;@class0		jsr readexit		pha		php		jsl unlock_mem		plp		pla		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDPclose_s		PROCNAME		;shell for the CLOSE call		import close		jsl lock_mem		ldx <g_fcr_ptr		;set up real pointers to vp's to fcr & vcr provided…		ldy <g_fcr_ptr+2	;…by the SCM		jsl deref		stx <fcr_ptr		sty <fcr_ptr+2		ldx <g_vcr_ptr		ldy <g_vcr_ptr+2		jsl deref		stx <vcr_ptr		sty <vcr_ptr+2check_pcnt;		lda class;		beq @class0;@class1;		WITH close1;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #pmax;		bcc @ok1;		lda #invalid_pcount;		sec;		bra exit;@ok1;		ENDWITH@class0do_close		ldy #fcr_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		cmp #$000F		;is it a directory?		beq free_fcr		;if directory file then don't release its buffer…					;…because it is shared with the VCR		ldy #fcr_buf_vp		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get fcr buffer's vp so we can release it		tax		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl release_segfree_fcr		ldy #fcr_ref_num		lda [fcr_ptr],y		jsl release_fcr		bcc @ok1		lda #invalid_ref_num OR $8000	;internal error		bra exit@ok1		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;get the open count		bne @ok2		;make sure open count isn't aleady 0		lda #8000		;generic internal error		bra exit@ok2		dec a			;one less open file		sta [vcr_ptr],yno_err				;successful close		clc		lda #$0000exit		pha		php		jsl unlock_mem		plp		pla		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDPget_dev_num_s	PROCNAME		;shell for the GET_DEV_NUM call		import open_setup		import match_vcr		import find_vol_online		;brk $09		;stz gen_buf_vp		;stz gen_buf_vp+2		jsl lock_memcheck_pcnt;		lda class;		beq @class0;@class1;		WITH get_dev_num1;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #pmax;		bcc @ok1;		lda #invalid_pcount;		sec;		bra exit;@ok1 ;		ENDWITH@class0check_scm				;see whether SCM has done the work for us yet		lda <dev1_num		;is the number there already?		beq hard_way		;if not, we have to figure it out ourselveseasy_way		ldy #get_dev_num1.dev_num	;anticipate class 1		ldx class		bne @store		;class 1, store the value@class0		ldy #get_dev_num0.dev_num@store		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		bra no_err		;that's the whole show!hard_way				;we have to find the volume ourselves		jsr open_setup		;init vars, set up buffers, put volume name in…					;…volname_buf_ptr		bcc @ok		cmp  #dup_volume	; duplicate volume?  if yes, that means that someone else					; will claim it...		bne  @1				lda  #unknown_vol@1		sec		bra exit		;return with error@ok		ldy #vcr_dev		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;get device number		bra easy_way		;we got it!;have_name			;check for vcr with the given name		;jsr match_vcr		;find vcr for volume name in volname_buf_ptr		;bcc @ok		;lda #vol_not_found		;bra exit		;return with error;@ok		;bne use_old_vcr		;if we got a match, use it		;stz supposed_dev		;jsr find_vol_online	;no vcr, walk the devices		;bcc @ok1		;lda #vol_not_found		;bra exit@ok1		;lda <drvr_dev_num	;the answer is here		;bra easy_way		;mail it and we're doneuse_old_vcr			;we have a vcr for the volume				;vcr_ptr points to it		;lda <dev1_num		;bra easy_wayno_err				;successful get_dev_num		clc		lda #$0000exit		pha		php		lda gen_buf_vp		tax		ora gen_buf_vp+2		beq @skip3		ldy gen_buf_vp+2		jsl release_seg@skip3		jsl unlock_mem		plp		pla		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDPget_eof_s	PROCNAME		;shell for the GET_EOF call		jsl lock_mem		ldx <g_fcr_ptr		;set up real pointers to vp's to fcr & vcr provided…		ldy <g_fcr_ptr+2	;…by the SCM		jsl deref		stx <fcr_ptr		sty <fcr_ptr+2;		ldx <g_vcr_ptr;		ldy <g_vcr_ptr+2;		jsl deref;		stx <vcr_ptr;		sty <vcr_ptr+2check_pcnt;		lda class;		beq @class0;@class1;		WITH get_eof1;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #pmax;		bcc @ok1;		lda #invalid_pcount;		sec;		bra exit;@ok1;		ENDWITH@class0do_get_eof		ldy #fcr_eof		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the eof (of all things)		tax		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;high word		pha			;save accum		lda class		beq @class0@class1		pla			;get back low word		ldy #get_eof1.eof+2		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		txa			;restore low word		dey		dey		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		bra no_err		;that's it!@class0		pla			;get back low word		ldy #get_eof0.eof+2		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		txa			;restore low word		dey		dey		sta [param_blk_ptr],yno_err		clc		lda #$0000exit		pha		php		jsl unlock_mem		plp		pla		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDPget_mark_s	PROCNAME		;shell for the GET_MARK call		jsl lock_mem		ldx <g_fcr_ptr		;set up real pointers to vp's to fcr & vcr provided…		ldy <g_fcr_ptr+2	;…by the SCM		jsl deref		stx <fcr_ptr		sty <fcr_ptr+2;		ldx <g_vcr_ptr;		ldy <g_vcr_ptr+2;		jsl deref;		stx <vcr_ptr;		sty <vcr_ptr+2check_pcnt;		lda class;		beq @class0;@class1;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #get_mark1.pmax;		bcc @ok1;		lda #invalid_pcount;		sec;		bra exit;@ok1;@class0do_get_mark		ldy #fcr_mark		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the mark (of all things)		tax		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;high word		pha			;save accum		lda class		beq @class0@class1		pla			;get back low word		ldy #get_mark1.position+2		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		txa			;restore low word		dey		dey		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		bra no_err		;that's it!@class0		pla			;get back low word		ldy #get_mark0.position+2		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		txa			;restore low word		dey		dey		sta [param_blk_ptr],yno_err		clc		lda #$0000exit		pha		php		jsl unlock_mem		plp		pla		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDPset_mark_s	PROCNAME		;shell for the SET_MARK call		;brk $EF		jsl lock_mem		ldx <g_fcr_ptr		;set up real pointers to vp's to fcr & vcr provided…		ldy <g_fcr_ptr+2	;…by the SCM		jsl deref		stx <fcr_ptr		sty <fcr_ptr+2;		ldx <g_vcr_ptr;		ldy <g_vcr_ptr+2;		jsl deref;		stx <vcr_ptr;		sty <vcr_ptr+2check_pcnt		lda class		beq @class0@class1		ldy #set_mark1.displacement		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta disp		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta disp+2;		lda p_cnt;		cmp #set_mark1.pmax;		bcc get_base		bra get_base;		lda #invalid_pcount;		sec;		brl exit;@ok1@class0		ldy #set_mark0.position		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta disp		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta disp+2		bra absolute		;class 0 displacement is always absoluteget_base			;fetch displacement from param block		ldy #set_mark1.base		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		beq absolute		;base = 0 --> mark = displacement		dec a		beq minus		;base = 1 --> mark = eof - displacement		dec a		beq add			;base = 2 --> mark = mark + displacement		dec a		beq subtract		;base = 3 --> mark = mark - displacementbad_base			;if we get here, base had an invalid value		lda #parm_range_err	;base is out of range		brl exit		;can't continueabsolute			;set mark to (displacement)		lda disp		sta new_mark		lda disp+2		sta new_mark+2		bra validate_new_mark	;make sure it's in range, and we're done!minus				;set mark to (eof - displacement)		ldy #fcr_eof		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get eof		sec		sbc disp		sta new_mark		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get high word of eof		sbc disp+2		bcs @no_underflow		lda #out_of_range	;position fell below 0		bra exit@no_underflow		sta new_mark+2		bra set_new_mark	;new mark is guaranteed to be valid nowsubtract			;set mark to (mark - displacement)		ldy #fcr_mark		lda [fcr_ptr],y		sec		sbc disp		sta new_mark		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get high word of present mark		sbc disp+2		bcs @no_underflow		lda #out_of_range	;mark would go below 0		bra exit@no_underflow		sta new_mark+2		bra set_new_mark	;new mark is guaranteed to be valid nowadd				;set mark to (mark + displacement)		ldy #fcr_mark		lda [fcr_ptr],y		clc		adc disp		sta new_mark		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get high word of mark		adc disp+2		bcc @no_overflow		lda #out_of_range	;new mark overflowed 32-bit range		bra exit@no_overflow		sta new_mark+2validate_new_mark		;check value of new mark against eof		lda new_mark+2		ldy #fcr_eof+2		cmp [fcr_ptr],y		;compare to high word of eof		bcc @in_range		bne @out_of_range@maybe				;now check low words		dey		dey		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get low word of eof		cmp new_mark		bcs @in_range@out_of_range		lda #out_of_range		bra exit@in_rangeset_new_mark		lda new_mark		ldy #fcr_mark		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;set new mark		lda new_mark+2		iny		iny		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;that completes the new mark setting!no_err		clc		lda #$0000exit		pha		jsl unlock_mem		pla		cmp #1		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exitdisp		ds.l 1			;local copy of user parameter "displacement"new_mark	ds.l 1			;scratch space for new mark value		ENDPflush_s		PROCNAME		;handle the FLUSH callcheck_pcnt			;this is about all we do?		lda class		beq @class0@class1		lda p_cnt		cmp #2+1		;max pcount for FLUSH is 2		bcc @ok1		lda #invalid_pcount		sec		bra exit@ok1@class0no_err		clc		lda #$0000exit		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDPfst_specific_s	PROCNAME		;shell for fst-specific calls		import set_text_mode		import get_text_mode		WITH fst_specific		ldy #command		lda [param_blk_ptr],y	;get command parameter		beq @bad_command	;0 not a valid command		dec a		bne @next1		jsr set_text_mode	;command = 1		bra exit@next1		dec a		bne @next2		jsr get_text_mode	;command = 2		bra exit@next2@bad_command			;command number not valid		lda #invalid_fst_op		secexit		cmp #1		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDWITH		ENDPnot_supported2	PROCNAME	;handle FST calls which are not supported because they require…				;…write operations				;this routine handles calls which take a pathname as a parameter				;if the pathname refers to a DOS 3.3 disk, we return an…				;…invalid_fst_op error				;if the pathname refers to a non-DOS 3.3 disk, we return a…				;…unknown_vol error, which allows the call to bounce to other…				;…FST's		import open_setup		;brk $AC		jsl lock_memcheck_volume			;the main thing is to know whom the volume belongs to		jsr open_setup		;this routine allocates a buffer, sets up name buffer…					;…pointers, parses the path provided by SCM, 		bcs pack_up		;return with unknown_vol, or pathalogical error@ok1		lda #drvr_wr_prot	;call was meant for uspack_up		pha		lda gen_buf_vp		tax		ora gen_buf_vp+2		beq @skip3		ldy gen_buf_vp+2		jsl release_seg@skip3exit		;brk $22		jsl unlock_mem		pla		cmp #1		bcc @noErr				ora error_priority@noErr		jml sys_exit		ENDP;======================================================================;Below is the main entry point for ALL standard operating system calls.;;This PROC was adapted directly from the ProDOS FST v02.00 by Rob Turner;;Input:         X = Call number * 2;               Y = Class number * 2;               A = undefined;======================================================================		longa	on		longi	on				EXPORT	appl_call	appl_call	PROCNAME		import	max_call		sta $FF0500		;debug tag		phk			;set up our bank register		plb		rep #$30		; 16 bit A & X		stz  p_cnt		; zero it out		stz  error_priority	; for bouncing errors		sty class		;keep this around for future reference		cpy #0		beq @class0@class1		lda [param_blk_ptr]	;first word of class1 is always pcount		sta p_cnt		;save for future reference				lda pcount_tbl,x	; get the min/max pcount for this call		sep #$20		; 8 bit accum. please		LONGA OFF		sta p_max_cnt		xba		sta p_min_cnt		lda p_cnt				cmp p_max_cnt		; Max pcount - pcount		bcs pcnt_err		; pcount too big		cmp p_min_cnt		; Min pcount - pcount		blt pcnt_err		; pcount too small		rep #$20		; back to 16 bit accu.		LONGA ON		@class0		stz gen_buf_vp		;invalidate vp's until buf gets allocated		stz gen_buf_vp+2		cpx #end_tbl+1		;check command number		bcs cmd_error		jmp (cmd_tbl,x)		;call the functionpcnt_err		; bad pcount in the call		rep #$20		; back to 16 bit accu.		LONGA ON		lda #invalid_pcount		bra errcmd_error		;bad command number, or not FST call				lda #bad_system_callerr		sec		ora error_priority		jml sys_exitnot_supported		;call not supported by this FST			;we get here if the call takes a ref num as a parameter, in…			;…which case we are certain the call was meant for this FST		lda #drvr_wr_prot		bra  errnot_implemented		; no handler for this call		lda #invalid_fst_op		bra  errcmd_tbl		dc.w	cmd_error	;undefined		00		DC.W	not_supported2	;CREATE			01		DC.W	not_supported2	;DESTROY		02		DC.W	cmd_error	;OS_SHUTDOWN		03		DC.W	not_supported2	;CHANGE_PATH		04		DC.W	not_supported2	;SET_FILE_INFO		05		DC.W	get_file_info_s	;GET_FILE_INFO		06		DC.W	not_implemented	;JUDGE_NAME		07		DC.W	volume_s	;VOLUME			08		DC.W	cmd_error	;SET_PREFIX		09		DC.W	cmd_error	;GET_PREFIX		0A		DC.W	not_supported2	;CLEAR_BACKUP		0B		DC.W	cmd_error	;SET_SYS_PREFS		0C		DC.W	cmd_error	;NULL			0D		DC.W	cmd_error	;EXPAND_PATH		0E		DC.W	cmd_error	;GET_SYS_PREFS		0F		DC.W	open_s		;OPEN			10		DC.W	cmd_error	;NEWLINE		11		DC.W	read_s		;READ			12		DC.W	not_supported	;WRITE			13		DC.W	close_s		;CLOSE			14		DC.W	flush_s		;FLUSH			15		DC.W	set_mark_s	;SET_MARK		16		DC.W	get_mark_s	;GET_MARK		17		DC.W	not_supported	;SET_EOF		18		DC.W	get_eof_s	;GET_EOF		19		DC.W	cmd_error	;SET_LEVEL		1A		DC.W	cmd_error	;GET_LEVEL		1B		DC.W	get_dir_entry_s	;GET_DIR_ENTRY		1C		DC.W	cmd_error	;BEGIN_SESSION		1D		DC.W	cmd_error	;END_SESSION		1E		DC.W	cmd_error	;SESSION_STATUS		1F		DC.W	get_dev_num_s	;GET_DEV_NUM		20		DC.W	cmd_error	;GET_LAST_DEV		21		DC.W	cmd_error	;READ_BLOCK		22		DC.W	cmd_error	;WRITE_BLOCK		23		DC.W	not_supported	;FORMAT			24		DC.W	not_supported	;ERASE_DISK		25		DC.W	cmd_error	;RESET_CACHE		26		DC.W	cmd_error	;GET_NAME		27		DC.W	cmd_error	;GET_BOOT_VOL		28		DC.W	cmd_error	;QUIT			29		DC.W	cmd_error	;GET_VERSION		2A		DC.W	cmd_error	;GET_FST_INFO		2B		DC.W	cmd_error	;D_INFO			2C		DC.W	cmd_error	;D_STATUS		2D		DC.W	cmd_error	;D_CONTROL		2E		DC.W	cmd_error	;D_READ			2F		DC.W	cmd_error	;D_WRITE		30		DC.W	cmd_error	;ALLOC_INT and BIND_INT	31		DC.W	cmd_error	;DEALLOC_INT and UNBIND_INT	32		DC.W	fst_specific_s	;FST_SPECIFIC		33		;EXPORT	end_tblend_tbl		equ * - cmd_tbl;=====================================================================; Below is the table used to check the pcount on the calls that are; not supported.  This should have been done in general for all the ; calls instead of doing it inline in each call.  Oh well I didn't; start this thing and "to each his own".  If I had time I would go back ; and change all the calls, but we're too close to beta to do it now.; jev	3/26/91;=====================================================================pcount_tbl	DC.W	cmd_error		DC.W	max_pcnt7+min_pcnt1	;CREATE			01		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;DESTROY		02		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;OS_SHUTDOWN		03		DC.W	max_pcnt3+min_pcnt2	;CHANGE_PATH		04		DC.W	max_pcnt12+min_pcnt2	;SET_FILE_INFO		05		DC.W	max_pcnt12+min_pcnt1	;GET_FILE_INFO		06		DC.W	max_pcnt6+min_pcnt1	;JUDGE_NAME		07		DC.W	max_pcnt6+min_pcnt2	;VOLUME			08		DC.W	max_pcnt2+min_pcnt2	;SET_PREFIX		09		DC.W	max_pcnt2+min_pcnt2	;GET_PREFIX		0A		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;CLEAR_BACKUP		0B		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;SET_SYS_PREFS		0C		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;NULL			0D		DC.W	max_pcnt3+min_pcnt2	;EXPAND_PATH		0E		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;GET_SYS_PREFS		0F		DC.W	max_pcnt15+min_pcnt2	;OPEN			10		DC.W	max_pcnt4+min_pcnt4	;NEWLINE		11		DC.W	max_pcnt5+min_pcnt4	;READ			12		DC.W	max_pcnt5+min_pcnt4	;WRITE			13		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;CLOSE			14		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;FLUSH			15		DC.W	max_pcnt3+min_pcnt3	;SET_MARK		16		DC.W	max_pcnt2+min_pcnt2	;GET_MARK		17		DC.W	max_pcnt3+min_pcnt3	;SET_EOF		18		DC.W	max_pcnt2+min_pcnt2	;GET_EOF		19		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;SET_LEVEL		1A		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;GET_LEVEL		1B		DC.W	max_pcnt17+min_pcnt5	;GET_DIR_ENTRY		1C		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;BEGIN_SESSION		1D		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;END_SESSION		1E		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;SESSION_STATUS		1F		DC.W	max_pcnt2+min_pcnt2	;GET_DEV_NUM		20		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;GET_LAST_DEV		21		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;READ_BLOCK		22		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;WRITE_BLOCK		23		DC.W	max_pcnt4+min_pcnt3	;FORMAT			24		DC.W	max_pcnt4+min_pcnt3	;ERASE_DISK		25		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;RESET_CACHE		26		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;GET_NAME		27		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;GET_BOOT_VOL		28		DC.W	max_pcnt2+min_pcnt0	;QUIT			29		DC.W	max_pcnt1+min_pcnt1	;GET_VERSION		2A		DC.W	max_pcnt8+min_pcnt2	;GET_FST_INFO		2B		DC.W	max_pcnt11+min_pcnt2	;D_INFO			2C		DC.W	max_pcnt5+min_pcnt5	;D_STATUS		2D		DC.W	max_pcnt5+min_pcnt5	;D_CONTROL		2E		DC.W	max_pcnt6+min_pcnt6	;D_READ			2F		DC.W	max_pcnt6+min_pcnt6	;D_WRITE		30		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;ALLOC_INT and BIND_INT	31		DC.W	max_pcnt0+min_pcnt0	;DEALLOC_INT and UNBIND_INT	32		DC.W	max_pcnt17+min_pcnt1	;FST_SPECIFIC		33				;EXPORT	pend_tblpend_tbl	equ * - pcount_tbl		ENDP;======================================================================;Below is the main entry point for ALL FST system calls;;This PROC was adapted directly from the ProDOS FST v02.00 by Rob Turner;;;Input:     X = Call number * 2;           Y = Class number * 2;           A = undefined;======================================================================		EXPORT	system_call	system_call	PROCNAME		sta $FF0510		;debug tag		phk			;setup our bank register		plb				cpx	#max_sys+1	;maximum system calls		bcs	sys_err		jmp	(sys_tbl,x)	;call system routinesys_err		lda	#bad_system_call		rtl			;return error to the SCMstartup		jsl get_sys_gbuf	;get pointer to general 1K buffer		stx gbuf_ptr		sty gbuf_ptr+2		lda #$0001		;set default text mode to clear high bits		sta text_flag		bra exitshutdowndeferred_flushexit		lda #$0000		clc		rtlsys_remove_vol			;clean up a vcr before SCM throws it away		sta >$FE0358		ldx <g_vcr_ptr		ldy <g_vcr_ptr+2		stx <vcr_ptr		sty <vcr_ptr+2		ldy #vcr_buf_vp		;point to vp for the segment owned by the vcr		lda [g_vcr_ptr],y	;g_vcr_ptr contains a real pointer		tax		iny		iny		ora [g_vcr_ptr],y	;check that it's not 0		beq @invalid_vp		lda [g_vcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl release_seg		;throw away the 4K buffer@invalid_vp		rtl			;return with any errorsys_tbl		dc.w	sys_err		DC.W	startup		;set ready for work		DC.W	shutdown	;get ready to quit		DC.W	sys_remove_vol	;remove local data from VCR		DC.W	deferred_flush	;flush deferred blocks.max_sys		equ	* - sys_tbl		ENDPmatch_vcr	PROCNAME	;given a volume name, try to find a matching vcr.				;volume name in volname_buf_ptr		import throw_away		import find_vol_online		import cmp_vol_vcr		;this is a complicated task, so here is the pseudocode:;	try to find a VCR with the same volume name;;		NOT FOUND: return with no match;;		FOUND:;			is it mine?;				NO: try to discard it (no open files);					SUCCESSFUL discard: return with no match;					CAN'T discard: return w/duplicate_vol error;;				YES: find the disk online, checking in dev_num or last known;					device (error if failure);;					is the disk really the same as one that VCR refers to?;						YES: return with match;						NO: try to discard it (no open files);							SUCCESSFUL discard: return with no match;							CAN'T discard: return w/dup_vol error				;check for vcr with same name		;brk $03		ldx <volname_buf_ptr		ldy <volname_buf_ptr+2		lda #$0000		;tell find_vcr to search by name		jsl find_vcr		;see if a vcr exists for this volume		bcc same_name		;same name, see if it's mineno_match		lda #0			;report no match		clc		rtssame_name		jsl deref		stx <vcr_ptr		sty <vcr_ptr+2		ldy #vcr_fst_id		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;see if it's mine		cmp #my_id		beq mine		jsr throw_away		bcc no_match		;successful discard, return no matchdup_vol				;return with error		lda #dup_volume		;duplicate volume		sec		rtsmine				;it's mine		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt	; <CAF> By incrementing the vcr open count, I		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y	; fool SCM into not throwing away the vcr for		inc  a			; this volume when the disk is accessed.		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y			lda <dev1_num		;was a device number given by SCM?		bne verify_same		;if so, see if the vcr matches the online disk					;no dev_num given, search devices starting with the…					;…one it was last seen in		ldy #vcr_dev		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;find where it was last seen		sta supposed_dev		jsr find_vol_online	;find the physical disk		bcc verify_same		;we found one, check it				ldy  #vcr_open_cnt	; <CAF> Restore the previous open count.		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		lda #vol_not_found		sec		rtsverify_same	;we have a disk with the same name, but let's check two full…		;…sectors' worth of data			ldy  #vcr_open_cnt	; <CAF> Restore the previous open count.		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		jsr cmp_vol_vcr		bcs try_discard		;it's not the same, try to get rid of the VCRmatch				;we have a match!		ldy #vcr_id		lda [vcr_ptr],y		clc		rts			;return with vcr_id in accumtry_discard		jsr throw_away		;try to throw away the incorrect vcr		bcs dup_vol		;can't, report duplicate volume		bra no_match		;otherwise, report no match		ENDP		export open_setupopen_setup	PROCNAME		;perform basic setup for OPEN and GET_FILE_INFO		import parse_path		import volume		import find_vol_online		import allocate_vcr		import cmp_vol_vcr		import device_id		stz supposed_dev	;init to 0		stz valid_vcr		stz gen_buf_vp		stz gen_buf_vp+2		lda #gen_buf_size	;let's get some buffer space for the vtoc & directory		jsl alloc_seg		bcc @ok		lda #out_of_mem		;can't get buffer space		rts@ok		stx gen_buf_vp		;4K buffer used by volume routine		sty gen_buf_vp+2		jsl deref		stx <gen_buf_ptr		sty <gen_buf_ptr+2		lda #name_buf		sta <volname_buf_ptr		lda #^name_buf		sta <volname_buf_ptr+2		lda #<file_buf		;get address of this internal buffer		sta <file_name_ptr		lda #^file_buf		sta <file_name_ptr+2		lda #<vol_name_buf	;get address of this internal buffer		sta <vol_name_ptr		lda #^vol_name_buf		sta <vol_name_ptr+2		;brk $12		jsr parse_path		;check path and break off filename and volume name		bcc @ok4		lda #bad_path_syntax		rts* <CAF> 11/08/90* ok, at this point we have allocated any buffers and broken down the pathname, and it* is a valid dos pathname.  now we must attempt to find the volume which is the target* of this call.  the target may actually belong to another FST, so this is what must* be done:** A. does a vcr exist?*  1. yes - *    a. is it DOS?*      1. yes -*        a. is it same volume?*          1. yes - verify that has not been switched.  *            a. if not switched, then done (goto B)*            b. if switched, start scanning from last seen device (goto A.2.a)*          2. no - if no open files, then proceed as if it was not DOS (goto A.1.b)*      2. no - act as if a vcr does not exist, so that if a volume is found, we can try*         to throw this vcr out (goto A.2.a)*  2. no -*    a. find the dos volume in one of the devices.  If the vcr exists, attempt to throw*       it out.  If it was thrown out, then create the new vcr for the dos volume.*       done. (goto B)* B. done*@ok4		lda <dev1_num		beq have_vol_name	;if 0 dev_num then we have our volume pointed…					;…to by volname_buf_ptr		sta <drvr_dev_num		jsr device_id		;check to see if this is a 5.25 device		bcs @exit		;failed to find the device		bne @exit		;can't deal with non-5.25 drives		jsr volume		;get name of volume in that device					;that routine will return a g-string in vol_name_ptr		bcc @ok5		;can't recognize volume@exit		sec		lda #unknown_vol		rts			;return with bouncing error@ok5		lda #<vol_name_buf		;this is our volume name for sure		sta <volname_buf_ptr		lda #^vol_name_buf		sta <volname_buf_ptr+2* A. does a vcr exist?have_vol_name		ldx  <volname_buf_ptr		ldy  <volname_buf_ptr+2		lda  #$0000		;tell find_vcr to search by name		jsl  find_vcr		;see if a vcr exists for this volume*  2. no -		bcs  find_vol		; no vcr, so go look for volume ->*  1. yes - same_name		jsl  deref		stx  <vcr_ptr		sty  <vcr_ptr+2		*    a. is it DOS?		ldy  #vcr_fst_id		; is it a vcr for a dos volume?		lda  [vcr_ptr],y		;		cmp  #my_id*      1. yes -		beq  mine		; yes ->		*      2. no - act as if a vcr does not exist, so that if a volume is found, we can try*         to throw this vcr out (goto A.2.a)lab112		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt	; no, any open files?		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		beq  find_vol		; no, so lets act as if I haven't seen the vcr, and go try					; to find a dos volume with the same name.** ok, I've found a vcr for a volume that has open files.  this means that even if* I were to find a dos volume of the same name, I couldn't mount it because of this volume.* that means that now I must return either dup_vol or vol_not_found.** dup_vol        ->  I found a dos volume online but couldn't mount it.* vol_not_found  ->  couldn't find a dos volume of this name.** what are the side effects of my just returning vol_not_found?* - won't be able to tell if a duplicate volume has been inserted**		stz  supposed_dev	; we have no clue what device it might be in		jsr  find_vol_online		lda  #vol_not_found	; assume that we couldn't find it		bcc  @1		brl  exit		; couldn't find it ->@1		lda  #dup_volume	; was found, so error is a dup_volume error		brl  exit		; ->** I've found a vcr for a dos volume.  check to see if it is the same volume.**        a. is it same volume?mine		ldy  #vcr_buf_vp	;set up correct buffer for check_dir		lda  [vcr_ptr],y		tax		iny		iny		lda  [vcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl  deref		stx  vol_buf_ptr		sty  vol_buf_ptr+2		jsr  cmp_vol_vcr	; same?		bcs  @not_same		; no ->*          1. yes - verify that has not been switched.  @same		ldy  #vcr_status		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		and  #vcr_swapped*            a. if not switched, then done (goto B)		beq  done		; not switched ->*            b. if switched, start scanning from last seen device (goto A.2.a)		ldy  #vcr_dev		; get the last device it was in		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		sta  supposed_dev		bra  find_vol2		; switched, so go find it ->*          2. no - if no open files, then proceed as if it was not DOS (goto A.1.b)@not_same	bra  lab112		; lab112 checks vcr_open_cnt ->*      2. no -*        a. find the (possibly) dos volume in one of the devices.  If the vcr exists, attempt to throw*           it out.  If it was thrown out, then create the new vcr for the dos volume.*           done. (goto B)find_vol				; we have a volume name, but make sure that it is a dos disk in					; one of the drives							stz  vcr_ptr		; zero out the vcr pointer so that I know if I only need to		stz  vcr_ptr+2		; update the device number		stz  supposed_dev	; start at first device		find_vol2	stz  myflag1		; assume no prior vcr		lda  vcr_ptr		; vcr?		ora  vcr_ptr+2		beq  @1			; no ->			inc  myflag1		; set flag indicating that I have bumped the open count		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt	; increment the open count so volume won't be lost		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y	; the only time that this might not work would be if we are		inc  a			; searching for a duplicate dos 3.3 volume, but that is not		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y	; very likely.@1		jsr  find_vol_online		php		pha				lda  myflag1		beq  @2				ldy  #vcr_open_cnt	; decrement the open count		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		stz  myflag1		@2		pla		plp		bcs  exit		; couldn't find it ->		lda  vcr_ptr		; found a volume, did we have a vcr already?		ora  vcr_ptr+2		beq  @alloc		; no, go create one ->			ldy  #vcr_dev		; yes, update the device number in the vcr		lda  drvr_dev_num		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y				ldy  #vcr_status	; clear the disk swapped flag		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		and  #$BFFF		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		bra  done		@alloc		jsr  allocate_vcr	; found volume, allocate the vcr		bcs  exit		; error ->* B. donedone		ldy  #vcr_dev		; setup the drvr_dev_num		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		sta  drvr_dev_num				clcexit		rtsmyflag1		dc.w	0		ENDP		export fill_paramfill_param	PROCNAME	;fill the user param list according to the table pointed to…				;…by fill_tabl.  p_cnt must be correct		ldy #$0000-2		;init index		ldx p_cnt		;keep countdown in x@cpy_loop		iny		iny			;move to next word entry		lda (fill_tabl),y	;get the table entry		asl a			;test 2 highest bits		php			;save the results in carry and neg flags		bmi @no_copy		;if original bit 14 was set, don't copy		lsr a			;shift things back into place		phy			;save the present index		tay		lda global_params,y		ply		sta [param_blk_ptr],y@no_copy		plp			;restore the first test result		bcc @cpy_loop		;should we decrement pcount?		dex			;decrement pcount		bne @cpy_loop		;if we're not done, keep looping@done		rts		;now we have the param list fill tables:		;table to specify what data to copy from the fcr to the user		;parameter block.  each position corresponds to the same position		;in the user parameter block.		;each word entry contains:		;	bit 15 = decrement pcount--high for the 1st word in each parameter		;	bit 14 = copy inhibit--if high, nothing gets copied for this word positionno_copy		equ %0100000000000000dec		equ %1000000000000000		;the label 'g' is short for 'global_params' and is the address of the start…		;…of the table of global parameters.  It is needed in the offset expression…		;…for each entry that represents a param to be copied, so I used a one-letter…		;…label for convenience.*************************************************************	EXPORT get_file_info0_fget_file_info0_f	dc.w no_copy				;pathname	dc.w no_copy	dc.w access		- g		;access	dc.w os_type		- g		;file_type	dc.w aux_type 		- g		;aux_type	dc.w null		- g	dc.w stor_type		- g		;storage_type	dc.w null		- g		;create_date	dc.w null		- g		;create_time	dc.w null		- g		;mod_date	dc.w null		- g		;mod_time	dc.w blks_used		- g		;blocks_used	dc.w null		- g	+ dec*************************************************************	EXPORT get_file_info1_fget_file_info1_f	dc.w no_copy				;pcount	dc.w no_copy				;pathname	dc.w no_copy			+ dec	dc.w access		- g	+ dec	;access	dc.w os_type		- g	+ dec	;file_type	dc.w aux_type		- g		;aux_type	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w stor_type		- g	+ dec	;storage_type	dc.w null		- g		;create_date_time	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w null		- g		;mod_date_time	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w no_copy				;option_list	dc.w no_copy			+ dec	dc.w eof		- g		;eof	dc.w eof+2		- g	+ dec	dc.w blks_used		- g		;blocks_used	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	;dc.w no_copy				;resource_eof	;dc.w no_copy			+ dec	;dc.w no_copy				;resource_blocks	;dc.w no_copy			+ dec;	Resource fork info now gets zeroed;	-- Monte Benaresh 2/19/92 for 6.0.1	dc.w null		- g		;resource_eof	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w null		- g		;resource_blocks	dc.w null		- g	+ dec*************************************************************	EXPORT volume0_fvolume0_f		;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT volume1_f	volume1_f		;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT open0_f	open0_f		;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT open1_fopen1_f		;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT read0_f	read0_f		;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT read1_f	read1_f		;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT close0_f	close0_f	;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT close1_f	close1_f	;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT set_mark0_f	set_mark0_f	;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT set_mark1_f	set_mark1_f	;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT get_mark0_f	get_mark0_f	;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT get_mark1_f	get_mark1_f	;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT get_eof0_f	get_eof0_f	;this call is mostly special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT get_eof1_f	get_eof1_f	;this call is mostly special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT get_dir_entry0_fget_dir_entry0_f	dc.w no_copy				;ref_num	dc.w no_copy				;flags	dc.w no_copy				;base	dc.w no_copy				;displacement	dc.w no_copy				;name	dc.w no_copy	dc.w entry_num		- g		;entry_num	dc.w os_type		- g		;file_type	dc.w eof		- g		;eof	dc.w eof+2		- g	dc.w blks_used		- g		;block_count	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g		;create_date_time	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g		;mod_date_time	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	dc.w access		- g		;access	dc.w aux_type		- g		;aux_type	dc.w null		- g	dc.w fst_id		- g	+ dec	;file_sys_id	*************************************************************	EXPORT get_dir_entry1_fget_dir_entry1_f	dc.w no_copy				;pcount	dc.w no_copy			+ dec	;ref_num	dc.w no_copy			+ dec	;flags	dc.w no_copy			+ dec	;base	dc.w no_copy			+ dec	;displacement	dc.w no_copy				;name	dc.w no_copy			+ dec	dc.w entry_num		- g	+ dec	;entry_num	dc.w os_type		- g	+ dec	;file_type	dc.w eof		- g		;eof	dc.w eof+2		- g	+ dec	dc.w blks_used		- g		;block_count	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w null		- g		;create_date_time	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w null		- g		;mod_date_time	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w access		- g	+ dec	;access	dc.w aux_type		- g		;aux_type	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w fst_id		- g	+ dec	;file_sys_id	dc.w no_copy				;option_list	dc.w no_copy			+ dec	;dc.w no_copy				;resource_eof	;dc.w no_copy			+ dec	;dc.w no_copy				;resource_blocks	;dc.w no_copy			+ dec;	Resource fork info now gets zeroed;	-- Monte Benaresh 2/19/92 for 6.0.1	dc.w null		- g		;resource_eof	dc.w null		- g	+ dec	dc.w null		- g		;resource_blocks	dc.w null		- g	+ dec*************************************************************	EXPORT get_dev_num0_f	get_dev_num0_f	;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************	EXPORT get_dev_num1_f	get_dev_num1_f	;this call is all special-case, so this routine never gets called for it.*************************************************************		ENDP;======================================================================;new_rwts	Read/write a given track/sector.;		Calculates: block = (16 * track) + sector; ;Enter:         JSR;;			sector	   |    track;Input:         A =|F|E|D|C|B|A|9|8|7|6|5|4|3|2|1|0|;			This is what you get if you do a 16-bit load on a;			track/sector entry typically found in a DOS 3.3;			data structure.;;               X = undefined;               Y = undefined;               P = nvmxdizc;                   ..000..0;               b = k;;Output:        A = undefined;               X = undefined;               Y = undefined;               P = nvmxdizc;                   ..000..|___ high = device error, low = successful;               b = k;;uses:	Good for reading sectors.; ;======================================================================		longa on		longi onnew_rwts	PROCNAME		;read/write a track/sector		xba			;switch track byte/sector byte		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF		asl a			;get sector nibble flush left in byte		asl a		asl a		asl a				rep #%00100000		;now open up to 16 bits		LONGA ON		lsr a		lsr a		lsr a		lsr a			;calculation done--we have a block number		sta <drvr_blk_num	;put on parm list		stz <drvr_blk_num+2	;clear high word;make this call	lda #drvr_read;more general	sta <drvr_call_num		lda #$0100		;256-byte "blocks"		sta <drvr_blk_size		sta <drvr_req_cnt	;we only deal in whole blocks…		stz <drvr_req_cnt+2	;…and only one at a time!		lda #my_id		sta <drvr_fst_num		stz <drvr_cache		;to hell with caching@retry		jsl dev_dispatcher	;go read		bcs @err		rts@err		cmp #drvr_disk_sw		beq @retry		sec		rts		ENDP	;======================================================================;find_fde	Find the file descriptive entry #n in catalog sector #k;		in vol_name_buf.;; ;Enter:         JSR;;;Input:         A = k, as in "catalog sector #k";;               X = n, as in "fde #n";               Y = undefined;               P = nvmxdizc;                   ..000..0;               b = k;;Output:        A = undefined;               X = undefined;               Y = undefined;               P = nvmxdizc;                   ..000..|___ high = error, low = successful;               b = k;		fde_ptr = longword pointer to first byte of that fde;;uses:; ;======================================================================find_fde	PROCNAME		;find a file descriptive entry		cmp #max_cat_sec+1	;see if in range		bcs @error		;range error		xba			;we now have a byte offset to start of that cat sector		adc #cat_strt_off	;add offset to first cat sector		adc #base_fde		;add base fde offset within catalog sector		cpx #max_fde+1		;check range		bcs @error@add		dex			;decrement fde offset		bmi @fde_done		;we're done when we get below zero--loop 0 or more times		adc #fde_len		;add byte length of each fde		bra @add@fde_done	;clc	hopefully, carry will be clear		adc vol_buf_ptr		;finished product is address of fde in contiguous…		sta fde_ptr		;…buffer of catalog sectors		lda vol_buf_ptr+2	;get high part		adc #$0000		sta fde_ptr+2		rts@error		rts		ENDP;======================================================================;; load_fde_flag (added 6-May-93 DAL);; This routine is similar to;   lda [fde_ptr];   and #$00ff; That first byte of an fde is $FF for a deleted entry.;; We also return $FF for a non-deleted entry if the filename is; all blanks, which would be a zero-length filename.;;Enter:         JSR;;;Input:         A = undefined;               X = undefined;               Y = undefined;               P = nvmxdizc;                   ..000...;               b = k;;		fde_ptr = points to a file-descriptive entry;;Output:        A = first byte of fde, or $FF if the filename is blanks;               X = preserved;               Y = preserved;               P = nvmxdizc;                   ..000.|.___ Z is conditioned for A;               b = k;;======================================================================load_fde_flag	PROC		lda [fde_ptr]		and #$00ff		beq @done	;beyond end of catalog--done		cmp #$00ff		beq @done	;a real deleted entry--done*** If all 30 filename characters are blank, simulate a deleted entry		phy		phx		ldx #15		ldy #fde_name@search		lda [fde_ptr],y		cmp #$A0A0	;blanks?		bne @nonBlank		iny		iny		dex		bne @search		lda #$00ff	;all blanks--simulate a deleted entry		bra @leave@nonBlank	lda [fde_ptr]@leave		plx		ply@done		and #$00FF		rts		ENDP;======================================================================;cmp_string	Compare two class 1 strings pointed to by str1 and str2.;		Str2 is masked with cmp_mask.  Maximum length is $8000;		bytes.; ;Enter:         JSR;;;Input:         A = undefined;               X = undefined;               Y = undefined;               P = nvmxdizc;                   ..000..0;               b = k;;		str1_ptr = longword pointer to one string, usually from GS/OS;		str2_ptr = longword pointer to other string, possibly with high bits set,;			   usually from DOS.  This string gets masked with cmp_mask.;		cmp_mask = 8-bit value to be ANDed with each character in str2.;;Output:        A = undefined;               X = undefined;               Y = undefined;               P = nvmxdizc;                   ..000..|___ high = compare false, low = compare true;               b = k;;uses:		Good for comparing two strings.; ;======================================================================			;let's try this using LONG accumulator!cmp_string	PROCNAME		;compare two strings		lda [str1_ptr]		;get string length		cmp [str2_ptr]		bne @different		;if they're not even the same length...		tay		bpl @ok		ldy #$7FFF		;in the unlikely event that y is greater than $7FFF, it…					;…is truncated to $7FFF@ok		iny			;point to last character		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF@loop		lda [str2_ptr],y	;y must be signed POSITIVE		and cmp_mask		;user mask, maybe to strip high bit?		cmp [str1_ptr],y		bne @different		dey		bpl @loop		rep #%00100001		;16-bit accum, carry clear		rts@different	sec		rep #%00100000		;16-bit accum		rts		LONGA ON				ENDPallocate_vcr	PROCNAME		;find old VCR or allocate new one for volume…					;…found by the "volume" subroutine		;enter with		;	volname_buf_ptr		points to volume name		import load_cat_secs		import find_vol_online		;brk $A4		;do we need to allocate a VCR for this volume?		jsr match_vcr		;find vcr for volume name in volname_buf_ptr		bcc @ok		lda #dup_volume		;return with duplicate_volume error		rts@ok		beq find_vol		;no match, find volume and allocate a new VCR		brl have_vcr		;if we got a match, don't allocate new VCRfind_vol		jsr find_vol_online	; supposed_dev is setup by the caller of allocate_vcr		bcc req_vcr		lda #vol_not_found		rtsreq_vcr		lda #vcr_size		;ldx #<vol_name_buf		;ldy #^vol_name_buf		ldx <volname_buf_ptr		ldy <volname_buf_ptr+2		jsl alloc_vcr		;brk $AA		bcc @ok		lda #out_of_mem		;can't get new vcr		rts			;return carry set@ok		jsl deref		stx <vcr_ptr		sty <vcr_ptr+2		lda #$8000		tsb vcr_fcr_flags	;set flag to say we allocated a VCRfill_new_vcr		lda gen_buf_vp		ora gen_buf_vp+2	;is there a valid buffer?		bne @have_gen_buf@get_gen_buf		lda #gen_buf_size	;let's get some buffer space for the vtoc & directory		jsl alloc_seg		bcc @got_buf		lda #out_of_mem		;can't get buffer space		bra vol_vcr_err@got_buf		stx gen_buf_vp		;4K buffer used by volume routine		sty gen_buf_vp+2@have_gen_buf		ldy #vcr_fst_id		lda #my_id		sta [vcr_ptr],y		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		;lda #$FFFF		;this value will prevent a swap-out, but we understand…					;…it to be 0		lda #0		sta [vcr_ptr],y		;set open count to 0 since we just allocated this vcr		ldy #vcr_dev		lda <drvr_dev_num	;where did we find the disk?		sta [vcr_ptr],y		ldy #vcr_buf_vp		;index to virtual pointer to vtoc & directory buffers		lda gen_buf_vp		;transfer the vp's for the general buffer…					;…to the vol_buf now that we know…					;…that we want to keep them		tax			;save for deref		sta [vcr_ptr],y		iny		iny		lda gen_buf_vp+2		sta [vcr_ptr],y		tay			;set up for deref		jsl deref		stx vol_buf_ptr		;set up for rest of the FST		sty vol_buf_ptr+2		stz gen_buf_vp		;nail the original vp's so that we know…		stz gen_buf_vp+2	;…not to release them laterload		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt	; prevent swap out of vcr		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		inc  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y				jsr load_cat_secs	;load catalog sectors into vol_buf				php		pha				ldy  #vcr_open_cnt	; restore original count		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y				pla		plp				bcc load_okvol_vcr_err		pha			;save error code@cancel_vcr		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		lda #$0000		sta [vcr_ptr],y		;must zero the open count to release it!		ldy #vcr_id		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;get ID of the VCR		jsl release_vcr		;this invokes sys_remove_vol call to this fst		lda #$8000		trb vcr_fcr_flags	;clear flag since we deallocated the VCR		pla			;restore error		sec		rtsload_ok		lda cat_sec_count	;enter catalog sector count into VCR		ldy #vcr_cat_sec_count		sta [vcr_ptr],y		bra vol_exithave_vcr				;update old VCR		ldy #vcr_buf_vp		;get the vcr's buffer set up		lda [vcr_ptr],y		tax		iny		iny		lda [vcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		stx vol_buf_ptr		sty vol_buf_ptr+2		ldy #vcr_dev		lda <drvr_dev_num	;where did we find the disk?		sta [vcr_ptr],yvol_exit		;lda gen_buf_vp		;we may have to release this segment		;tax			;save in case it's valid		;ora gen_buf_vp+2	;null vp?		;beq @skip3		;ldy gen_buf_vp+2		;jsl release_seg		;release unused gen buf@skip3		clc		rts			;that's all, folks!		ENDPvolume		PROCNAME		;check a device for a valid DOS 3.3 disk					;caller must set device in drvr_dev_num					;returns a volume name in vol_name_ptr					;carry set means that a DOS 3.3 disk was…					;…not found.				lda <gen_buf_ptr		sta <drvr_buf_ptr		lda <gen_buf_ptr+2		sta <drvr_buf_ptr+2		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		lda #$0011		;get VTOC, always at track 17, sector 0		jsr new_rwts		;make driver call		bcc @ok		rts			;return error@ok			;so, is it a DOS volume?		;brk 99		sep #$30		;work with bytes		LONGI OFF		LONGA OFF		ldx #id_tbl_end-id_values-1	;point to last entry in id tables@loop1		lda id_offset,x		;get offset into VTOC		tay@loop2		lda [drvr_buf_ptr],y	;get the actual value		cmp id_values,x		;compare to the table value		bne @false		;not the same@loop3		dex		bmi confirmed		;table finished		tya		cmp id_offset,x		;skip over other entries for same position		beq @loop3		bra @loop1		;move on to next compare@false		dex		bmi @failed		tya		cmp id_offset,x		;see if there's an alternate value for that offset		beq @loop2		;yes, get a second chance@failed		sec				rep #$30		;word accum		LONGA ON		LONGI ON		lda #unknown_vol	;return bouncing error		rts			;sorry, not a DOS volumeconfirmed		;well, it looks like a DOS 3.3 volume!				rep #$31		;word accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		LONGI ON				;now we must load the first directory sector!		ldy #vtoc_cat_link	;get the link to first catalog sector		lda [drvr_buf_ptr],y		bne @ok		lda #dir_error		;this is a weird error		rts@ok		pha			;save this for a minute		lda <drvr_buf_ptr		sta <gen_buf_ptr		clc		adc  #$0100		;bump by a page		sta <drvr_buf_ptr		lda <drvr_buf_ptr+2		sta <gen_buf_ptr+2		adc #$0000		sta <drvr_buf_ptr+2		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		pla			;get back the track/sector		jsr new_rwts		;read the sector		bcc @ok1;		lda #error		;device error		rts@ok1generate_name			;now generate the name		ldy #$01FE		;point to end of area to be checksummed		lda #$0000		;seed the checksum		clc			;this is part of the seed@loop		eor [gen_buf_ptr],y		ror a			;scramble bits		bpl @1			;random condition		eor #$7FFF		;conditional flip of all but high bit@1		dey		dey		bpl @loop			;we now have a 16-bit checksum in the accumulator		sta chksum;		and #$F800		;take the high five bits;		lsr a;		lsr a			;use it as an index into word table;		xba;		tax		ldx #0			;we no longer use the table of names		lda name_tabl,x		;this table contains word pointers to 2 bytes…		sta <namegen_ptr	;…before name stringscopy_alpha		;now copy the alphabetic part of the generated name to the buffer		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF		ldy #$0002		;we need this offset for the g-string@loop		lda (namegen_ptr),y		beq @done		sta (vol_name_ptr),y		iny		cpy #alpha_len_limit	;just in case, we don't want to overflow our buffer		bne @loop@done				rep #%00100000		LONGA ONbcd		stz bcd_result		;we're going to do a BCD calculation		stz bcd_result+2	;1 *byte*/digit		lda chksum		and #$07FF		;get lowest 11 bits		sta bin_temp@1000		sec		sbc #1000		bcc @100		sta bin_temp		lda bcd_result		adc #$1-1		;carry is set		sta bcd_result		lda bin_temp		bra @1000@100		lda bin_temp		sec		sbc #100		bcc @10		sta bin_temp		lda bcd_result		adc #$100-1		;carry is set		sta bcd_result		bra @100@10		lda bin_temp		sec		sbc #10		bcc @almost_done		sta bin_temp		lda bcd_result+2		adc #$1-1		;carry is set		sta bcd_result+2		bra @10@almost_done		;brk $ED		lda bin_temp		xba		adc bcd_result+2	;take care of ones place.  carry is clear		sta bcd_result+2				;we should now have the bcd value of lower 11 bits of the checksum in bcd_result.		lda bcd_result		adc #'00'		;get ascii for this digit.  carry is clear.		sta (vol_name_ptr),y		iny		iny		lda bcd_result+2		adc #'00'		;get ascii for this digit.  carry is clear.		sta (vol_name_ptr),y		iny		iny		lda #$0000		sta (vol_name_ptr),y@done2			dey		dey			;adjust to find name length		tya		sta (vol_name_ptr)	;this completes the g-string;we are done generating the name				rep #$31		;long accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		LONGI ON				lda #$8000		sta error_priority	;any error now has priority				rts;	1/4/91	jev	Removed table of volume names.  It was felt that it would not be;			appropriate to use the names from Prinston and that just DOS 3.3;			was what was aggreed on.name_tabl		;this table contains word pointers to 3 bytes before the name strings		dc.w name1 - 2;		dc.w name2 - 2;		dc.w name3 - 2;		dc.w name4 - 2;		dc.w name5 - 2;		dc.w name6 - 2;		dc.w name7 - 2;		dc.w name8 - 2;		dc.w name9 - 2;		dc.w name10 - 2;		dc.w name11 - 2;		dc.w name12 - 2;		dc.w name13 - 2;		dc.w name14 - 2;		dc.w name15 - 2;		dc.w name16 - 2;		dc.w name17 - 2;		dc.w name18 - 2;		dc.w name19 - 2;		dc.w name20 - 2;		dc.w name21 - 2;		dc.w name22 - 2;		dc.w name23 - 2;		dc.w name24 - 2;		dc.w name25 - 2;		dc.w name26 - 2;		dc.w name27 - 2;		dc.w name28 - 2;		dc.w name29 - 2;		dc.w name30 - 2;		dc.w name31 - 2;		dc.w name32 - 2		;now we have the actual name data:		string Cname1		dc.b 'DOS 3.3 v'; name2		dc.b 'HAMILTON'; name3		dc.b 'DOD'; name4		dc.b 'HENRY'; name5		dc.b 'EDWARDS'; name6		dc.b 'HOLDER'; name7		dc.b 'WITHERSPOON'; name8		dc.b 'PYNE'; name9		dc.b 'SPELMAN'; name10		dc.b 'MCCOSH'; name11		dc.b 'WOOLWORTH'; name12		dc.b 'PALMER'; name13		dc.b 'JADWIN'; name14		dc.b 'DILLON'; name15		dc.b 'PROSPECT'; name16		dc.b 'ALEXANDER'; name17		dc.b 'FINE'; name18		dc.b 'EQUAD'; name19		dc.b 'FIRESTONE'; name20		dc.b 'MATHEY'; name21		dc.b 'NASSAU'; name22		dc.b 'KRESGE'; name23		dc.b 'MCCORMICK'; name24		dc.b 'CLAPP'; name25		dc.b 'WAWA'; name26		dc.b 'TI'; name27		dc.b 'CHARTER'; name28		dc.b 'ELM'; name29		dc.b 'COLONIAL'; name30		dc.b 'QUAD'; name31		dc.b 'TERRACE'; name32		dc.b 'CAMPUS'id_offset		;these are offsets into the VTOC of bytes which are checked in order			;to determine whether a disk is DOS 3.3 format:		dc.b $3		;DOS release #		dc.b $27	;# of T/S pairs per T/S list sector		dc.b $36,$37	;# of bytes per sector		dc.b $31,$31	;direction of track allocation (2 possible values)		dc.b $34,$34	;# of tracks per disk (2 possible values??)		dc.b $35,$35	;# of sectors per track (2 possible values??)id_values		;these are the actual values required for a DOS 3.3 disk:		dc.b 3		;DOS release #		dc.b $7A	;# of T/S pairs per T/S list sector		dc.b $00,$01	;# of bytes per sector		dc.b $01,$FF	;direction of track allocation (2 possible values)		dc.b 35,50	;# of tracks per disk (2 possible values??)		dc.b 16,32	;# of sectors per track (2 possible values??)id_tbl_end			;storage areachksum		ds 1bin_temp	ds 1bcd_result	ds.l 1		ENDPthrow_away	PROCNAME		;try to throw away the current vcr		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;see if I can throw this away		beq go_ahead		sec			;we can't throw it away		rtsgo_ahead	ldy #vcr_id		lda [vcr_ptr],y		jsl release_vcr		clc		rts		ENDPcmp_vol_vcr	PROCNAME		;compare vcr buffers to region read in by "volume" routine		ldy #vcr_buf_vp		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;set up some real pointers to this vcr's buffers		tax		iny		iny		lda [vcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		stx <ptr1		sty <ptr1+2		;we are now ready to compare buffers		ldy #$01FE		;set index for compare@loop2		lda [vol_buf_ptr],y	;get word from VOLUME routine		cmp [ptr1],y		;match with word from VCR		bne @different		;if any difference, go on to next dev		dey		dey		bpl @loop2@same		clc	;if we get this far then they're identical		rts@different		sec		rts		ENDPdevice_id	PROCNAME		;get the device ID of given device					;on entry:					;	<drvr_dev_num must contain the number of the device					;on exit:					;	carry clear: Accumulator contains device ID					;	carry set: Accumulator contains device error	if 0 then		lda #drvr_status		sta <drvr_call_num		lda #$0002		sta <drvr_req_cnt	;we'd like just a word		stz <drvr_req_cnt+2		lda #ptr1 OR direct_base	;use this direct-page loc for the lousy 2 bytes		sta <drvr_slist_ptr		stz <drvr_slist_ptr+2		stz <drvr_stat_code	;$0000 means get device status		jsl dev_dispatcher		bcc @ok		rts			;return with driver error@ok		ldy #$34		;offset to device ID in DIB		lda [drvr_dib_ptr],y	;get the device id		rts	else		lda <drvr_dev_num		pha			;save for restoration		sta <drvr_buf_ptr	;store for dispatcher's use		stz <drvr_dev_num	;call the dispatcher directly		lda #$0001		;call to get_dib_ptr		sta <drvr_call_num		jsl dev_dispatcher	;call the dispatcher		ply			;restore device number		sty <drvr_dev_num		bcs @done		;just punt on error		ldy #$34		;offset to device ID in DIB		lda [drvr_dib_ptr],y	;get the device id@done		rts	endif		ENDPfind_vol_online	PROCNAME	;look for a volume in online devices			;enter with:			;	volume name as g-string in volname_buf_ptr			;	supposed_dev contains the number of the device where we expect…			;	…to find the volume or 0 to walk all devices		;brk $05		ldx supposed_dev		bne recover_loop	;this is the case where we look for a lost disksimple_loop				;this is the easy case: walk the device list@dev_loop		inx		stx <drvr_dev_num		jsr volume		;who's in that drive?		bcc @chk_name		;my disk, verify that it's the right name		cmp #invalid_dev_num	;see if out of devices		;bne @next		beq not_found		;end of devs@next		ldx <drvr_dev_num	;restore		bra @dev_loop@chk_name		lda volname_buf_ptr	;set up pointers for cmp_string		sta <str1_ptr		lda volname_buf_ptr+2		sta <str1_ptr+2		lda vol_name_ptr		sta <str2_ptr		lda #^vol_name_buf		sta <str2_ptr+2		lda #$00FF		sta cmp_mask		;bit mask for ASCII characters		jsr cmp_string		;are the names the same?		bcc found		;right disk!		stz error_priority	;wrong disk, clear the error proirity				bra @next		;look for anotherrecover_loop			;find a lost disk		stx <drvr_dev_num	;start with the suspected location. X contains supposed_dev		jsr device_id		;get that device's ID		bcc @ok		rts			;return with driver error@ok		sta dev_id		;save this value@loop		jsr volume		bcc @chk_name2		cmp #invalid_dev_num	;see if out of devices		bne @next2@wrap		stz <drvr_dev_num	;wrap down to start of list@next2		ldx <drvr_dev_num		inx		cpx supposed_dev	;have we come full circle?		beq not_found		;if so, we're done		stx <drvr_dev_num		jsr device_id		;get that device's ID		bcc @ok1		cmp #invalid_dev_num		beq @wrap		rts			;return with driver error@ok1		cmp dev_id		;same type of device?		beq @loop		bra @next2		@chk_name2		lda volname_buf_ptr	;set up pointers for cmp_string		sta str1_ptr		lda volname_buf_ptr+2		sta str1_ptr+2		lda vol_name_ptr		sta str2_ptr		lda #^vol_name_buf		sta str2_ptr+2		lda #$00FF		sta cmp_mask		jsr cmp_string		;are the names the same?		bcs @next2		;wrong diskfound			;right disk		clc		rtsnot_found	lda  #vol_not_found		sec		rtsdev_id		ds 1		ENDPsearch_fcr	PROCNAME	;find an fcr by name in file_name_ptr				;checks that fcr belongs to vcr in vcr_ptr		stz old_fcr		;if we find a dup fcr, we'll save its number here		stz fcr_index		;walk the fcr'sloop		inc fcr_index		lda fcr_index		jsl get_fcr		bcs not_found		;no match@ok1		jsl deref		stx old_fcr_ptr		sty old_fcr_ptr+2		ldy #fcr_fst_id		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y	;is it mine?		cmp #my_id		bne loop		ldy #fcr_vcr_id		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		ldy #vcr_id		cmp [vcr_ptr],y		;does it belong to the right volume?		bne loop		ldy #fcr_type		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y	;get filetype		cmp #$000F		;is it a directory file?		beq loop		ldy #fcr_path_name		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		;get virtual pointer to the pathname		tax		iny		iny		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		stx src_scratch		sty src_scratch+2parse					;now parse off file name		sep #$20		longa off		ldy #4-1		;start with second valid character@loop2		iny		lda [src_scratch],y		cmp #':'		;look for colon before filename		bne @loop2		ldx #2-1		;init ptr to dest string@loop3		iny			;now copy filename to scratch buffer		inx		lda [src_scratch],y		sta scratch_str_buf,x		bne @loop3		;if last character wasn't null, keep going		rep #$30		longa on		txa			;get final pointer		dec a		dec a			;adjust to string length		sta scratch_str_buf	;set length		ldx #<scratch_str_buf		ldy #^scratch_str_buf		stx <str2_ptr		sty <str2_ptr+2			;now set up for compare and see if the name matches		lda <file_name_ptr		sta <str1_ptr		lda #^file_buf		sta <str1_ptr+2		jsr cmp_string		bcs loop		;try next fcr in vcr's list			;at this point, we've found an fcr for a previous open of this file		lda fcr_index		sta old_fcr@found_exit		clcnot_found		rts		ENDPparse_path	PROCNAME	;parse off the path1 string into volume and filename.				;outputs are g-strings pointed to by volname_buf_ptr (vol name)…				;…and file_name_ptr.  These strings will contain null length…				;…words if they do not exist.				;this proc also checks length and syntax and returns…				;…with carry set if they are not valid.		lda <path_flag		and #$4000		;make sure path1 is valid		bne @continue@null		rep  #$30		; ensure 16bit mode		lda #$0000		;null out the strings		ldy #$0001		sta [volname_buf_ptr],y	;this takes care of the terminator nulls		sta (file_name_ptr),y		sta [volname_buf_ptr]	;this takes care of the length words		sta (file_name_ptr)		clc		rts@continue							sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF		ldy #$0002		;start of path1 string after length word		lda [path1_ptr],y	;get char		beq @null		;if terminator, set strings to null		cmp #':'		bne filename0		vol					;parse volume name@loop		iny		lda [path1_ptr],y		beq vol_end		;null means end of path string		cmp #':'		beq vol_end		;colon means end of the volume name		dey			;adjust for destination index		sta [volname_buf_ptr],y		iny			;adjust back		cpy #vol_max_char+3	;over the volume name length limit?		bcc @loopvol_end		dey			;index past last char in dest		lda #$00		sta [volname_buf_ptr],y	;place terminator		rep #%00100001		;clear carry as well		LONGA ON		tya		sbc #2-1		;adjust for length.  carry is clear		sta [volname_buf_ptr]	;set the length word		iny		lda [path1_ptr],y	;refresh my memory...		and #$00FF		bne filename		lda #$0000		;null out the strings		ldy #$0001		sta (file_name_ptr),y	;there is no filename		sta (file_name_ptr)		; We need to check to see if there might be a second pathname and if it might be bad.; We do this because we are a good FST and we need to return the right error for calls; like change path.check2		lda path_flag		and #path2_mask		; is there a second path		bne check_path2		; if so check it out.		clc		rtsbad_span	sec		rtscheck_path2	lda span2		beq bad_span		cmp #$001F		; carry is set if too big.		rtsfilename0	dey			;adjustmentfilename		ldx #$0002		stx temp_index		;this will be our index to the destination string		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF@loop		iny		lda [path1_ptr],y		beq fn_end		cmp #':'		beq error		;sorry, can't have subdirectories!		tyx			;save source index		ldy temp_index		;get dest index		cmp #','		bne @not_comma		lda #':'		;translate commas to colons@not_comma		sta (file_name_ptr),y		iny		cpy #fn_max_char+4		bcs error		sty temp_index		txy		bra @loopfn_end		ldy temp_index		sta (file_name_ptr),y	;accum contains zero		rep #%00100000		LONGA ON		tya		dec a		dec a			;adjust for length		sta (file_name_ptr)	;set length word		bra check2		;we're done with path1, now check path 2error		rep #%00100000		LONGA ON		sec		rtstemp_index	ds 1		ENDPfind_eof	PROCNAME	;find the eof and aux_type for a file on an online volume	;on entry:	;		volume's directory must be in vol_buf_ptr	;		dev_num must be set up	;		accum should contain T/S of first T/S list sector	;on exit:	;		X = eof (low)	;		Y = eof (high)	;	;	for Text, A-, B-, S-types:	;		A = total number of sectors used	;	;	for Bin, Asoft, Int, Rel	;		A = aux_type		ldx <fcr_buf_ptr	;set up buffer for driver		stx <drvr_buf_ptr		ldx <fcr_buf_ptr+2		stx <drvr_buf_ptr+2		stz data_secs_cnt		stz ts_secs_cnt		stz eof_scratch		stz eof_scratch+2				;load sectors with useful info -->T/S list & 1 data sect		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		inc  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		jsr new_rwts		;read in 1st T/S list sector		php		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		plp				bcc @ok1		rts			;return with driver error@ok1		lda dos_type		;this should contain the dos filetype		beq text		;text may be sparse		and #$0017		;check for "easy" types: Int, Asoft, Bin, Rel		beq not_easy		brl easy		;go handle easy typesnot_easy@count		ldy #ts_list_start	;point to start of t/s list entries		inc ts_secs_cnt		;count T/S list sector@loop		lda [drvr_buf_ptr],y	;get the entry		beq @empty		inc data_secs_cnt	;keep count of actual blocks used		iny		iny			;next entry		cpy #$0100		bne @loop		;get next unless we overflowed		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		ldy #ts_link		;offset in T/S sector to link bytes		lda [fcr_buf_ptr],y	;get the links		beq @done		;$0000 means no more links --> last T/S list sector		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		inc  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		jsr new_rwts		;load next T/S list		php		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		plp		bcc @count		;if good, count valid t/s entries		rts			;return with driver error@empty@done				;assume file is all bytes in all allocated sectors				;calculate: eof = (sectors used) * 256		lda data_secs_cnt	;get the number of data sectors used		xba			;multiply low byte by 256		tax			;save this value		and #$FF00		;clear (former) high byte		sta eof_scratch		txa			;get back that flipped sector count		and #$00FF		;now we want the other half		sta eof_scratch+2	;all done!		lda data_secs_cnt		clc		adc ts_secs_cnt		;find total number of sectors used		brl eof_exittext@count		ldx #ts_list_start	;init offset to 1st entry in case all are 0					;** Monte Benaresh -- 2/20/92		ldy #ts_list_start	;point to start of T/S list entries		inc ts_secs_cnt		;count T/S list sector@loop		lda [drvr_buf_ptr],y	;get the entry		beq @empty		tyx			;save in case it's the last non-zero		inc data_secs_cnt@empty		iny		iny			;next entry		cpy #$0100		bne @loop		;get next unless we overflowed		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		ldy #ts_link		;offset in T/S sector to link bytes		lda [fcr_buf_ptr],y	;get the links		beq @done		;$0000 means no more links --> last T/S list sector		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		inc  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		jsr new_rwts		;next t/s list		php		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		plp		bcc @count		;if good, count valid t/s entries		rts			;return with driver error@done			;we have the last T/S list sector for a text file.get_eof			;now we have to find the last valid (non-0) sector in the list		txa			;get that entry position so we can calculate		sec		sbc #ts_list_start	;subtract the offset to start of T/S list		lsr a			;divide by 2 to get # of sectors		xba			;turn it into a byte value		sta eof_scratch		;store temporary result = # of bytes in all but last…					;…data sector in this T/S list		lda <drvr_buf_ptr		adc #$0100		;incr bufer ptr to next pg. carry should be clear		sta <drvr_buf_ptr		bcc @no_carry		inc <drvr_buf_ptr+2@no_carry		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		txy			;restore the index		lda [fcr_buf_ptr],y		sta last_data_sec	;save this number in case we're successful;;	next added 2/20/92 by Monte Benaresh		bne @real_sector@no_sector		ldy #-1			;will get incremented to 0 for eof		bra found_eof		;calculate now@real_sector;	end 2/20/92		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		inc  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		jsr new_rwts		;load in that last data sector		php		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		plp		bcc @ok;		lda #error		return with driver error		rts@ok		;may need special check for case where data fills last sec exactly!		ldy #$00FF		;offset to last byte				sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF@loop2		lda [drvr_buf_ptr],y		bne found_eof		;when we hit a non-0, that's eof-1		dey			;back up to next one		bpl @loop2		;keep going as long as we don't hit bottom					;if we hit bottom, just set eof to end at end of last…					;…sector.  in effect this causes the fst to ignore the…					;…zero-filled sector.found_eof	rep #%00100001		;clear carry, too		LONGA ON		iny			;eof points to *next* byte		tyx			;save that byte part		ldy #ts_sec_offset	;offset to offset number of 1st sector in this list		lda [fcr_buf_ptr],y	;get sector offset word		xba		tay		and #$FF00		;keep high part --> byte offset		adc eof_scratch		;build this value.  carry is clear from above		sta eof_scratch		tya		and #$00FF		;this is byte offset for the high word		adc eof_scratch+2	;build high word with carry from low word		sta eof_scratch+2		txa			;get back that last byte part		adc eof_scratch		;carry should be clear		sta eof_scratch		lda eof_scratch+2		adc #$0000		sta eof_scratch+2				;find blks_used		lda data_secs_cnt		clc		adc ts_secs_cnt		;find total number of sectors used		bra eof_exit		easy				;filetypes Asoft, Int, Bin, and Rel contain their eof's!		lda <drvr_buf_ptr		clc		adc #$0100		;incr buffer ptr to next pg.		sta <drvr_buf_ptr		lda <drvr_buf_ptr+2		adc #$0000		;carry bank		sta <drvr_buf_ptr+2		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		ldy #ts_list_start	;offset to start of list entries		lda [fcr_buf_ptr],y	;get first data sector		sta last_data_sec		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		inc  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		jsr new_rwts		;load in that last data sector		php		pha		phy		ldy  #vcr_open_cnt		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		dec  a		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y		ply		pla		plp		bcc @ok;		lda #error		return with driver error		rts@ok		lda dos_type		ldy #$0000		;offset to length bytes for Applesoft & Integer		and #≈$FF83		;mask out Applesoft, Integer and lock bits		beq @get_len		;get the length bytes		ldy #$0002		;offset for binary and relocatable@get_len		lda [drvr_buf_ptr],y		sta eof_scratch		;that's the eof, period.		lda #$0000		sta eof_scratch+2	;never a high word for these filetypes@get_aux			;find the aux type		lda dos_type		and #≈$FF84		;mask out Binary		beq @bin		cmp #$0001		;is it integer?		bne @apsoft		lda #$0C00		bra eof_done@apsoft		lda #$0801		bra eof_done@bin		lda [drvr_buf_ptr]	;for reloc & binary, 1st word is aux_type!		eof_done	;we now have the eof, for every type, stored safely in eof_scratcheof_exit	ldx eof_scratch		ldy eof_scratch+2	;load eof into X & Y for caller				;on exit, A should contain either aux_type or blks_used		clc		rtseof_scratch	ds.l 1data_secs_cnt	ds 1ts_secs_cnt	ds 1		ENDPload_cat_secs	PROCNAME	;load the catalog sectors into vol_buf_ptr, up to…				;…max of 15 total				;at this point, the vtoc and the first catalog sector				;have been read in by the subroutine "volume"		lda <vol_buf_ptr		clc		adc #$0100		;set to first cat sector		sta <drvr_buf_ptr		lda <vol_buf_ptr+2		adc #$0000		;carry bank		sta <drvr_buf_ptr+2		ldx #14			;max number of additional cat sectors		stx countdn@loop		ldy #$0001		;offset to LINK BYTES in LAST CAT SECTOR		lda [drvr_buf_ptr],y	;get track/sector of next cat sector		beq @cat_done		;last cat sector					;range checking?		pha		lda <drvr_buf_ptr		adc #$0100		;bump to next sector.  carry should be clear		sta <drvr_buf_ptr		lda <drvr_buf_ptr+2		adc #$0000		;carry bank		sta <drvr_buf_ptr+2		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		pla			;restore track/sector request		jsr new_rwts		;go get it		bcc @ok;		lda #error		return with driver error		rts@ok		dec countdn		bne @loop@cat_done		lda #15		sec		sbc countdn		;total # of cat sectors		sta cat_sec_count	;this is the number of catalog sectors read in		clc		rtscountdn		ds 1		ENDPcheck_dir	PROCNAME	;check the directory sectors in vol_buf_ptr for…				;…the filename in file_name_ptr		lda file_name_ptr		sta str1_ptr		lda #^file_buf		sta str1_ptr+2		lda #$0000		;cat sector numbers start at 0@cat_loop	ldx #$0000		;same for fde's@fde_loop	sta cat_index		stx fde_index			;save these		jsr find_fde		bcc @ok;		lda #parm_range_err OR $8000	;internal range error		rts			;error@ok*** changed 6-May-93 DAL;;;		lda [fde_ptr]		;first byte tells whether in use;;;		and #$00FF		jsr load_fde_flag*** end 6-May-93		beq file_not_here	;a $00 means beyond last entry		cmp #$00FF		beq @next_fde		;inactive, go to next one		lda <fde_ptr		adc #fde_name-2		;add offset to name field w/room for length word.					;carry should be clear		sta <str2_ptr		lda <fde_ptr+2		adc #$0000		;carry bank		sta <str2_ptr+2		ldy #$1D+2		;offset to last character in name		lda [str2_ptr]		;save this word before we crash it with length		pha				sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF@loop		lda [str2_ptr],y	;borrow this pointer before we give it to cmp_string		cmp #' ' OR $80		;check for spaces used as padding (w/high bit set)		bne @nam_end		dey		bpl @loop		;as long as we don't hit bottom, keep going;		lda #dir_error		;name is all spaces!		plx		rep #$30		;long a,x		sec		rts@nam_end		dey			;adjust to string length		lda #$7F		sta cmp_mask		;set the compare mask		rep #%00100000		LONGA ON		tya		sta [str2_ptr]		;str2 is a g-string without the terminator		jsr cmp_string		;str1_ptr should contain file_name_ptr		pla			;restore that one word we stepped on		sta [str2_ptr]		bcc right_fde		;we got it!@next_fde	ldx fde_index		lda cat_index		inx			;next fde		cpx #$0007		;check limit of 7 fde's per cat sector		bcc @fde_loop		;we're ok, check next fde		ina			;next catalog sector		cmp cat_sec_count	;past our limit?		bcc @cat_loop		;move on to next cat sectorfile_not_here		;file not on this volume		lda #$FFFF		sta fde_index		;indicate file not found		clc		rtsright_fde	clc			;success		rts		ENDP		export do_option_listdo_option_list	PROCNAME	;return option list data to user buffer				;enter with:				;	Y = offset in param block to option list ptr		;brk $05		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2		ora <user_ptr		;test for 0		beq done		;if $00000000, don't use it!list_good		lda [user_ptr]		;get length word		cmp #4+2		;need 4 bytes for overhead, 2 for data		bcs @ok@too_small		sec			;this is an error		rts@ok		lda #my_id		; my id is same as its length = 2		tay		sta [user_ptr],y		iny		iny 			;offset to actual buffer		sta [user_ptr],y	;give user our FST IDdone		clc		rts			;that's all there is to it!		ENDP		export set_text_modeset_text_mode	PROCNAME	;handle FST-specific call		WITH fst_specific		lda p_cnt		cmp #3			;check pcount		beq @pcount_ok		lda #invalid_pcount		sec		rts@pcount_ok		ldy #param1		;get parameter		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		cmp #1+1		;range check		bcc @mode_ok@bad_mode		lda #parm_range_err		sec		rts@mode_ok		sta text_flag		lda #0			;no error		clc		rts		ENDWITH		ENDP		export get_text_modeget_text_mode	PROCNAME	;handle FST-specific call		WITH fst_specific		lda p_cnt		cmp #3			;check pcount		beq @pcount_ok		lda #invalid_pcount		sec		rts@pcount_ok		lda text_flag		ldy #param1		;get parameter		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		lda #0			;no error		clc		rts		ENDWITH		ENDPget_file_info	PROCNAME	;get all necessary info for a file and stuff it into…				;…global variables				;fde_ptr must point to the file's fde		lda #storage_type	;if it's not the root directory, it gets this storage type		sta stor_type		ldy #fde_type		lda [fde_ptr],y		;get the filetype		tax		and #$0080		;look at the lock bit		bne @locked		lda #access_unlocked		bra @store@locked		lda #access_locked@store		sta access		txa			;get back original fetch		and #$007F		;mask out high byte and lock bit		sta dos_typetranslate_type		;determine corresponding filetype		ldx #8@loop		lsr a		bcs @lookup		dex		bne @loop@lookup		txa		asl a			;multiply by two for table		tax		lda type_table,x		sta os_type		lda dos_type		and #$0017		;is it basic, Bin, or Rel?		beq not_easyeasy		ldy #fde_ts_link		lda [fde_ptr],y		;find_eof needs this		jsr find_eof		bcc @ok		rts			;return with driver error@ok		sta aux_type		stx eof		sty eof+2		ldy #fde_sec_used		lda [fde_ptr],y		;we can trust the directory for these filetypes		sta blks_used		clc		rtsnot_easy		ldy #fde_ts_link		lda [fde_ptr],y		;find_eof needs this		jsr find_eof		bcc @ok		rts			;return with driver error@ok		sta blks_used		stx eof		sty eof+2		stz aux_type		rts			;carry is cleartype_table		;lookup table to translate DOS filetypes to GS/OS(TM);				 GS/OS type			DOS 3.3 type;				 ----------			------------	dc.w $04	;	ASCII Text File			Text	dc.w $0F	;	Directory			(undefined)	dc.w $00	;	uncatgegorized			B-type	dc.w $00	;	uncatgegorized			A-type	dc.w $FE	;	EDASM Relocatable Code File	Relocatable	dc.w $00	;	uncatgegorized			S-type	dc.w $06	;	Binary File			Binary	dc.w $FC	;	Applesoft Basic Program		Applesoft Basic	dc.w $FA	;	Integer Basic Program		Integer Basic	dc.w $EE	;	Classic Auto			E-type		ENDPget_dir_entry	PROCNAME		;brk $1C		ldy  #vcr_dev		; even if we don't access the device, set this up		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y	; for get_last_dev.		sta  drvr_dev_num				stz error		;we store the non-fatal error here		ldy #fcr_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;SCM promises to give me the right fcr		cmp #$000F		;is it a directory file?		beq @ok		lda #version_error OR $8000	;internal error		sec		rts@ok		lda class		beq @class0@class1			ldy #get_dir_entry1.base		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		;get the base		sta base1		ldy #get_dir_entry1.displacement		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		;get displacement		sta displacement1		ldy #get_dir_entry1.name	;copy pointer to direct page		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2		bra chk_entry			;go validate the entry num@class0		ldy #get_dir_entry0.base		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		;get the base		sta base1		ldy #get_dir_entry0.displacement		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		;get displacement		sta displacement1		ldy #fcr_blks_used		lda [fcr_ptr],y			;get number of sectors owned by this directory		dea				;account for vtoc		sta cat_sec_count		;we need this below		ldy #get_dir_entry0.name	;copy pointer to direct page		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2		;brk $1dchk_entry		lda base1		tax			;save for a moment		ora displacement1	;are they both zero?		beq special		;special funtion for base = displacement = 0		txa			;restore original base value		beq absolute		dea		beq add		dea		beq subtract		lda #parm_range_err		rtsspecial				;base and displacement are both zero		ldy #fcr_tot_ent		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the total number of valid entries		sta entry_num		;user gets this value here		lda #0		ldy #fcr_entry_num		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;reset entry number for this directory		brl fill_param_blk	;that all we do!absolute		ldy #fcr_tot_ent		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the total number of valid entries		cmp displacement1		bcs @ok		lda #end_of_dir		;entry number too high		sec		rts@ok		lda displacement1		sta entry_num		bra find_entryadd		ldy #fcr_entry_num		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the current entry number		clc		adc displacement1		sta entry_num		ldy #fcr_tot_ent		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the total number of valid entries		cmp entry_num		;range check		bcs find_entry		lda #end_of_dir		sec		rtssubtract		ldy #fcr_entry_num		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the current entry number		dec  a		cmp  displacement1		bcc  @err		; out of range, displacement would make entry < 1		inc  a		sec		sbc displacement1		sta entry_num		ldy #fcr_tot_ent		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the total number of valid entries		cmp entry_num		;range check		bcs find_entry		@err		lda #end_of_dir		sec		rtsfind_entry			;cycle through to nth directory entry		lda entry_num		ldy #fcr_entry_num		sta [fcr_ptr],y		sta countdown		;set this up for the loop		ldy #vcr_buf_vp		;get the vcr's buffer set up		lda [vcr_ptr],y		tax		iny		iny		lda [vcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		stx vol_buf_ptr		sty vol_buf_ptr+2				;now loop through valid entries		lda #$0000		;cat sector numbers start at 0@cat_loop		ldx #$0000		;same for fde's@fde_loop		sta cat_index		stx fde_index		;save these		jsr find_fde		bcc @ok		rts			;error@ok*** changed 6-May-93 DAL;;;		lda [fde_ptr]		;first byte tells whether in use;;;		and #$00FF		jsr load_fde_flag*** end 6-May-93		bne @cont		;a $00 means beyond last entry		lda #end_of_dir OR $8000	;internal error		sec		rts@cont		cmp #$00FF		beq @inactive		;inactive, don't count it		dec countdown		beq right_fde		;if countdown hits 0, we've got our man@inactive		ldx fde_index		lda cat_index		inx			;next fde		cpx #$0007		;check limit of 7 fde's per cat sector		bcc @fde_loop		;we're ok, check next fde		ina			;next catalog sector		cmp cat_sec_count	;past our limit?		bcc @cat_loop		;move on to next cat sectorright_fde			;fde_ptr now points to the fde in question!				;now, alas, we have to go to disk for some of the info		ldy #vcr_name		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;get the vp's to volume name		tax		iny		iny		lda [vcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		stx volname_buf_ptr		sty volname_buf_ptr+2		ldy #vcr_dev		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;get last known device		sta supposed_dev		jsr find_vol_online		bcc @ok		lda #vol_not_found	;we must have the device online		rts@ok		ldy  #vcr_dev		; has the volume moved?		lda  [<vcr_ptr],y		cmp  drvr_dev_num		beq  @ok1		; no ->				ldy  #vcr_dev		; update the dev_num		lda  drvr_dev_num		sta  [<vcr_ptr],y@ok1		jsr get_file_info		bcc @ok2		lda #dir_error		rts@ok2				;we now have all our file info in global variablesdo_name		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF		ldy #fde_sec_used-1	;this points to the last byte of the filename@loop		lda [fde_ptr],y		cmp #' ' OR $80		;is it a space?		bne @set_len		;if not, we've found the last character		dey		bne @loop		;use bne just in case...@set_len		rep #%00100001		;16-bit accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		iny			;get past end		sty src_end		tya		sbc #fde_name-1		;adjust for name len.  note: carry is clear		sta name_len		ina		ina		ina			;add three		tay		lda [user_ptr]		sta usr_len		;this will be a worthwile investment		cpy usr_len		bcc @big_enough		lda #buff_too_small		sta error		;non-fatal@big_enough		ldy #fde_name-1		;this is our source pointer		lda #$0004-1		sta dest_ptr		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF@loop1		iny		cpy src_end		beq @name_done		ldx dest_ptr		inx		cpx usr_len		;check for end of user buffer		beq @name_done		stx dest_ptr		lda [fde_ptr],y		tyx		ldy dest_ptr		and #$7F		;strip high bits		cmp #':'		bne @not_colon		lda #','		;replace colons with commas@not_colon		sta [user_ptr],y		txy			;restore source pointer		bra @loop1@name_done		rep #%00100001		;16-bit accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		lda name_len		ldy #$0002		sta [user_ptr],y	;that sets the length wordfill_param_blk			;now fill in the user param block		lda class		bne @class1@class0		lda #$0000		ldy #get_dir_entry0.flags		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		;indicate not extended file		lda #$0001		sta p_cnt		;this will make the fill_param tables work right		lda #<get_dir_entry0_f		sta <fill_tabl		;set up for right parameter fill table		jsr fill_param		bra all_done			;now take care of the name@class1			lda #$0000		;non_extended file		ldy #get_dir_entry1.flags		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		lda #<get_dir_entry1_f		sta <fill_tabl		;set up for right parameter fill table		jsr fill_param		lda p_cnt		cmp #15			;do we need option list?		bcc @no_list		ldy #get_dir_entry1.option_list		jsr do_option_list		bcc @list_ok		lda #buff_too_small		sta error@no_list@list_okall_done		lda error		cmp #$0001		;set carry		rtssrc_end		ds 1dest_ptr	ds 1error		ds 1base1		ds 1displacement1	ds 1countdown	ds 1name_len	ds 1usr_len		ds 1		ENDPread_newline	PROCNAME	;transfer a range of bytes according to newline				;pointer at src_scratch must be set to the start of the…				;…source range				;pointer at usr_ptr must be set to destination buffer				;byte_cnt must contain the maximum number of bytes…				;…to be transferred				;recent_xfer gets updated				;on exit, carry set means a newline character was encounterednewline		ldy #fcr_newline	;get the newline pointer		lda [fcr_ptr],y		tax		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		stx nl_list_ptr		sty nl_list_ptr+2		ldy #fcr_mask		lda [fcr_ptr],y		sta <nl_msk		lda nl_len		;how many nl characters are we dealing with?		dea		bne slow_nl		;if more than 1 newline char, things slow downfast_nl		lda [nl_list_ptr]		and #$00FF		;there's only one real byte there		sta <nl_char		ldy byte_cnt		beq end_nl2		;check for degenerate case		ldy  #0		sep #$30		;short registers and accumulator		LONGA OFF		LONGI  OFF		@loop		phy		rep  #$30		LONGA  ON		LONGI  ON		ldy #fcr_dos_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the DOS 3.3 filetype		sep  #$30		LONGA  OFF		LONGI  OFF		bne @1			;if NOT 0 (TEXT file) don't touch the data		ply		lda  [<src_scratch],y	; xfer char		sta  [<user_ptr],y		and  #$7F		; strip the high bit for newline compare		bra  @2			; continue ->@1		ply		lda [src_scratch],y		sta [user_ptr],y@2		inc  recent_xfer		and <nl_msk		cmp <nl_char		beq @hit_nl				rep  #$30		LONGA  ON		LONGI  ON		iny		cpy  byte_cnt		sep  #$30		LONGA  OFF		LONGI  OFF				bcc  @loop				rep #$30		;16-bit accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		LONGI ON		clc		bra end_nl@hit_nl		rep #$30		;16-bit accum		LONGA ON		LONGI  ON		sec			;indicate that newline was encountered		bra end_nlslow_nl		ldy #$0000		sep #$20		;short accumulator		LONGA OFF		@loop		phy		rep  #$20		LONGA  ON		ldy #fcr_dos_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the DOS 3.3 filetype		sep  #$20		LONGA  OFF		bne @1			;if NOT 0 (TEXT file) don't touch the data		ply		lda  [<src_scratch],y	; xfer char		sta  [<user_ptr],y		and  #$7F		; strip the high bit for newline compare		bra  @2			; continue ->@1		ply		lda [src_scratch],y		sta [user_ptr],y@2		inc  recent_xfer		and <nl_msk		tyx				ldy nl_len@cmp_loop	dey		bmi @not_end		;we've run out of newline characters		cmp [nl_list_ptr],y		bne @cmp_loop		bra @hit_nl		;we've hit a newline character		@not_end	txy			;restore buffer position		iny		cpy byte_cnt		;are we out of bytes anyway?		bne @loop		rep #$20		;16-bit accum		LONGA ON		clc				bra end_nl@hit_nl		sec			;indicate that newline was encounteredend_nl		rep  #$30		LONGA  ON		LONGI  ONend_nl2		rts		ENDPread		PROCNAME		;handle the READ call		stz error		;errors go here		stz bytes_sent		stz bytes_sent+2				stz recent_xfer		;brk $42find_offset			;figure out what the "data_offset" value is for this file		ldy #fcr_dos_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		beq @pure_data		;0 means text		and #≈$0003		;mask off bits for Asoft & Integer		bne @not_basic		lda #$0002		;basic files have 2 bytes before the real data		sta data_offset		bra fetch_fcr@not_basic		and #≈$0014		;bits for binary & relocatable		bne @not_bin		lda #$0004		;these types have 4 bytes before real data		sta data_offset		bra fetch_fcr@not_bin@pure_data			;the only types left are considered to have pure data		stz data_offsetfetch_fcr			;fetch stuff from fcr for handy reference		ldy #fcr_mask		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get newline mask		sta nl_msk		ldy #fcr_newline_len		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get newline list length		sta nl_len		ldy #fcr_eof		lda [fcr_ptr],y		sta eof		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		sta eof+2		ldy #fcr_mark		lda [fcr_ptr],y		sta mark		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		sta mark+2		ldy #fcr_buf_vp		;set up the pointer to the buffers		lda [fcr_ptr],y		tax		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		stx <fcr_buf_ptr		sty <fcr_buf_ptr+2		;txa		lda class		beq @class0@class1		ldy #read1.request_count		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta req_cnt		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta req_cnt+2		ldy #read1.data_buffer		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2		bra @fetch_done@class0		ldy #read0.request_count		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta req_cnt		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta req_cnt+2		ldy #read0.data_buffer		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2@fetch_donecheck_mark			;must return error if mark = eof		lda mark		cmp eof		bne @not_equal		lda mark+2		cmp eof+2		bne @not_equal		lda #end_of_file		sta error		brl store_tcount		;return transfer count and exit@not_equalcheck_limits		;brk $A1		lda mark		clc		adc req_cnt		sta endmark		lda mark+2		adc req_cnt+2		bcs @too_big		;overflowed 32 bits!		sta endmark+2		cmp eof+2		bcc limit_ok		bne @too_big@maybe		lda eof		cmp endmark		bcs limit_ok@too_big		;lda #end_of_file		;sta error		;remember, it's non-fatal		lda eof+2		sta endmark+2		lda eof		sta endmark		;that's as far as we can go!limit_ok				;now calculate needed scratch values		lda endmark		sec		sbc mark		sta bytes_left		;this is the maximum number of bytes left to transfer		lda endmark+2		sbc mark+2		sta bytes_left+2	;this is the transfer count based on lesser of…					;…request count and (eof minus mark)		lda mark		clc		adc data_offset		sta phys_mark		;this is the "mark" for disk sectors		lda mark+2		adc #$0000		sta phys_mark+2		ldy #fcr_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;check for directory file		cmp #$000F		bne @normal		brl directory_file	;some weirdo wants to read the directory file@normalinit_drvr			;initialize direct page driver vars		ldy #vcr_dev		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;where did we see the disk last?		sta <drvr_dev_num	;we'll trust this number for now		lda #drvr_read		;set up for reading sectors		sta <drvr_call_num				;now we have to locate the t/s list sector we needfind_sector			;this is the return point for the big sector loop				;bytes_sent, bytes_left, and phys_mark should be updated…				;…before iterating		;brk $49		lda phys_mark		xba		and #$00FF		;this is now low byte of sector num which contains mark		sta sec_num		lda phys_mark+2		xba		tax		and #$FF00		ora sec_num		sta sec_num		txa		and #$00FF		sta sec_num+2		;this completes a 24-bit value for sec_num		;lda phys_mark		;ldy #$0000check_ts		lda fcr_buf_ptr		;t/s list sectors go here		sta drvr_buf_ptr		lda fcr_buf_ptr+2		sta drvr_buf_ptr+2		lda sec_num		ldy #ts_sec_offset		sec		sbc [fcr_buf_ptr],y	;do we have the right t/s list?		bcc start_over		;the one we have is too far, start from top		cmp #122		;are we within the range of the one we want?		bcc have_ts		;if the difference is less than the capacity of a…					;…t/s list, then we have the right onewalk_ahead		ldy #ts_link		lda [fcr_buf_ptr],y		bne @ok1		lda #dir_error		;the linked list is bad		sec		rts@ok1		jsr new_rwts		;go get that next t/s list sector		bra check_tsstart_over		ldy #fde_ts_link	;start from the first t/s list sector		lda [fde_ptr],y		;get the track/sector of first t/s list sector		jsr new_rwts		bcc @ok		rts			;return with driver error@ok		bra check_tshave_ts		;brk $43				;the accumulator contains the t/s entry offset number		asl a			;convert to word offset		adc #ts_list_start	;carry is clear		tay		lda [fcr_buf_ptr],y	;get the entry		bne @real		;if non-0 then it's a real sector		brl null_sect		;if the entry is zero, hopefully it's because we've hit…					;…a null portion of a sparse file@real		sta data_sect		;save entry		ldy #fcr_data_sect		cmp [fcr_ptr],y		;is our sector already there?		beq xfer_data		;if it is, skip the driver call!		lda nl_msk		;is newline mode set?		bne double_buf		;if so, we have to bite the bullet on this one!		lda phys_mark		and #$00FF		;look at least sig byte		bne double_buf		;are we sector aligned?		lda bytes_left		cmp #$101		bcc double_buf		;if user gets partial sector, must double buffersingle_buf			;read the puppy right into the user's buffer!		lda user_ptr		sta drvr_buf_ptr		lda user_ptr+2		sta drvr_buf_ptr+2		lda data_sect		;this was from the t/s list		jsr new_rwts		bcc @ok1		rts			;return with driver error@ok1		lda #$0100		sta recent_xfer		;this is what we've transfered		brl next_sector		;we're done with this sectordouble_buf		lda <fcr_buf_ptr		clc		adc #$100		;second page of buffer is for data sectors		sta drvr_buf_ptr		lda <fcr_buf_ptr+2		adc #$0000		sta drvr_buf_ptr+2		lda data_sect		jsr new_rwts		;read in the sector		bcc @ok		rts			;return with driver error@ok		ldy #fcr_data_sect		lda data_sect		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;make a record that we have this sector in the fcr bufferxfer_data		lda phys_mark			and #$00FF		;this is the physical start position		sta sec_start		;save for later		ldy bytes_left+2		bne @rest_of_sec	;if this isn't 0, we're definitely going to the end of…					;…this sector		clc		adc bytes_left		;find physical end position		cmp #$0100+1		;does it go past the end of the sector?		bcc @store@rest_of_sec		lda #$0100@store		sta sec_end		;the physical end position for this particular sector		sec		sbc sec_start		;now we have the number of bytes to be transfered…					;…from this sector		sta byte_cnt		lda sec_start		;get back least significant byte of start addr		clc		adc #$0100		;bump to second page of fcr buffer		adc <fcr_buf_ptr		sta <src_scratch		lda <fcr_buf_ptr+2		adc #$0000		sta <src_scratch+2		ldx nl_msk		bne newline		;go do it the ugly way		;brk $47		lda byte_cnt		;this is the # of bytes to be moved from this sector		cmp #move_info_be	;check transfer value against the break-even point…					;…for using the move_info callmy_move		bcs use_mi		lsr a			;divide by 2		tax		bcc @even		;if no remainder, go move by word					;otherwise we transfer the odd byte		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF		lda [src_scratch]		sta [user_ptr]		;that takes care of the blasted odd byte!		rep #%00100001		;16-bit accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		inc src_scratch		bne @no_carry		inc src_scratch+2@no_carry		inc user_ptr		bne @no_carry2		inc user_ptr+2@no_carry2@even		txa			;this is a word count		dea			;decrement effectively by 2 to point to the word		bmi @done		asl a		tay@loop		lda [src_scratch],y		sta [user_ptr],y		dey		dey		bpl @loop@done				;transfer complete!		lda byte_cnt		sta recent_xfer		;the whole amount was transferred		lsr a			;did we increment user_ptr earlier?		bcc next_sector		;no, no need to fix it up...		lda user_ptr		;else we must decrement it once to account for		bne @1			; the increment that we did above (for odd-size		dec user_ptr+2		; move)@1		dec user_ptr		;This ensures proper math when we update the pointer		bra next_sector		; at the end of the loop.use_mi				;use move_info		pei src_scratch+2	;high word of source pointer		pei src_scratch		;low word  "     "      "		pei user_ptr+2		;destination		pei user_ptr		pea $0000		;high word of transfer count is always 0		lda byte_cnt		pha		pea move_sinc_dinc	;command word		jsl move_info		bcc @ok1		lda #$8000		;internal generic error		rts@ok1		lda byte_cnt		sta recent_xfer		;the whole amount was transferred		bra next_sectornewline		jsr read_newline		bcc next_sector		;we ran out of bytes, so get more				lda recent_xfer		clc		adc bytes_sent		sta bytes_sent		bcc @no_carry		inc bytes_sent+2		@no_carry	clc			; all done, so compensate for the subtraction that		lda  bytes_sent		; is performed during post_process for newline mode.		adc  data_offset		sta  bytes_sent		lda  bytes_sent+2		adc  #0		sta  bytes_sent+2		brl post_process	;we hit a newline char, so return to callernext_sector			;at this point, only recent_xfer should reflect what has been…				;…sent to the caller		lda recent_xfer		clc		adc bytes_sent		sta bytes_sent		bcc @no_carry		inc bytes_sent+2@no_carry		lda bytes_left		sec		sbc recent_xfer		sta bytes_left		bcs @no_borrow		dec bytes_left+2		@no_borrow	lda  bytes_left		; done?		ora  bytes_left+2		bne  @1			; maybe ->				clc			; all done, so compensate for the subtraction that		lda  bytes_sent		; is performed during post_process for newline mode.		adc  data_offset		sta  bytes_sent		lda  bytes_sent+2		adc  #0		sta  bytes_sent+2		brl  post_process							; if in newline mode, then it will go negative when					; it is done, but only by the amount of data_offset...@1		lda  bytes_left		; check to see if there are any more bytes to xfer.		clc			; must add the data_offset or else the value may be		adc  data_offset	; < 0.		sta  @temp		lda  bytes_left+2		adc  #0		ora  @temp				bne @more		;no more bytes left to transfer!		brl post_process		@temp		dc.w	0@more		lda recent_xfer		tax			;save for other calculations		clc		adc phys_mark		;update the physical mark		sta phys_mark		bcc @no_carry1		inc phys_mark+2@no_carry1		txa			;get back recent_xfer		clc		adc user_ptr		;update user_ptr		sta user_ptr		bcc @no_carry3		inc user_ptr+2@no_carry3		brl find_sector		;we're set to iteratenull_sect		lda nl_msk		beq @no_nl		;no newline if mask is 0		ldy nl_len		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF@loop		dey		bmi @no_nl		lda [nl_list_ptr],y	;determine whether 0 is on the newline list		bne @loop		;fall through on a zero		sta [user_ptr]		;store the single zero in user's buffer		rep #%00110001		;16-bit accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		inc bytes_sent		bne @no_carry		inc bytes_sent+2@no_carry		lda bytes_left		sec		sbc #$0001		sta bytes_left		bcs @no_borrow		dec bytes_left+2@no_borrow		brl post_process	;all done!@no_nl		rep #%00110001		;16-bit accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		lda phys_mark			and #$00FF		;this is the physical start position		sta sec_start		;save for later		ldy bytes_left+2		bne @rest_of_sec	;if this isn't 0, we're definitely going to the end of…					;…this sector		clc		adc bytes_left		;find physical end position		cmp #$0100+1		;does it go past the end of the sector?		bcc @store@rest_of_sec		lda #$0100@store		sta sec_end		;the physical end position for this particular sector		sec		sbc sec_start		;now we have the number of bytes to be transfered…					;…from this sector		sta byte_cnt		lsr a			;divide by 2		tax		lda #$0000		;null sectors contain zeros		bcc @even		;if no remainder, go move by word		sep #%00100000		;work with bytes		LONGA OFF		sta [user_ptr]		;that takes care of the blasted odd byte!		rep #%00100001		;16-bit accum, carry clear		LONGA ON		inc user_ptr		bne @no_carry2		inc user_ptr+2@no_carry2@even		txa			;this is a word count		dea			;decrement effectively by 2		bmi @done		asl a			;make it a byte value again		tay		lda #$0000@loop1		sta [user_ptr],y		dey		dey		bpl @loop1@done		lda byte_cnt		sta recent_xfer		;the whole amount was transferred		brl next_sectordirectory_file			;read stuff from the directory file		lda nl_msk		;is newline mode set?		beq dir_no_nl		;if not, just shove the bytes over@newline		lda bytes_left		sta byte_cnt		;only one word should be non-zero		stz byte_cnt+2		lda mark		clc		adc fcr_buf_ptr		sta src_scratch		lda mark+2		adc fcr_buf_ptr+2		sta src_scratch+2		jsr read_newline		lda recent_xfer		sta bytes_sent		stz bytes_sent+2	;high word is always 0		bra post_process	;that's all there is to it!dir_no_nl		lda mark		;get back least significant word of start addr		clc		adc fcr_buf_ptr		tax		lda mark+2		adc fcr_buf_ptr+2		pha			;high word of source pointer		phx			;low word  "     "      "		pei user_ptr+2		pei user_ptr		pea $0000		;high word of transfer count is always 0		lda bytes_left		pha		pea move_sinc_dinc	;command word		jsl move_info		bcc @ok1		lda #$8000		;internal generic error		rts@ok1		lda bytes_left		sta bytes_sent		;the whole amount was transferred		lda bytes_left+2		sta bytes_sent+2		;brl post_process		bra  pack_up		; don't strip high bits on directory data ->		post_process	sec			; subtract the data_offset from the amount		lda  bytes_sent		; actually transferred.		sbc  data_offset		sta  bytes_sent		lda  bytes_sent+2		sbc  #0		sta  bytes_sent+2					;clear high bit of each byte sent, if specified by mode		ldy #fcr_dos_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get the DOS 3.3 filetype		bne pack_up		;if NOT 0 (TEXT file) don't touch the data@text		lda text_flag		;this global flag decides the text transfer mode		beq pack_up		;if flag = 0, leave text as-is		;bra pack_up		;shunt-out this code for the time being		lda class		beq @class0@class1		ldy #read1.data_buffer		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2		bra @clear_bit@class0		ldy #read0.data_buffer		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr		iny		iny		lda [param_blk_ptr],y		sta <user_ptr+2@clear_bit		ldy bytes_sent+2		iny			;adjust for countdown		ldx bytes_sent		bne @not_0		dey			;account for low part = 0		txa		ora bytes_sent+2	;are they both zero?		beq @done@not_0		sty <clear_ctr		;this is the high part of the counter		ldy #0			;init index		sep #$20		LONGA OFF@loop		lda [user_ptr],y		and #$7F		;clear that archaic high bit		sta [user_ptr],y	;put it back		iny			;bump ptr		bne @no_carry1		inc <user_ptr+2		;bump high part of pointer@no_carry1		dex			;low part of counter		bne @loop		dec <clear_ctr		;high part of counter		bne @loop@done		rep #$20		LONGA ONpack_up				;square away all the values for the user param block before…				;…returning				;bytes_sent should reflect the total amount transfered during…				;…the entire call		ldy #fcr_mark		lda [fcr_ptr],y		clc		adc bytes_sent		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;update the file's mark		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		adc bytes_sent+2		sta [fcr_ptr],ystore_tcount		lda class		bne @class1@class0		ldy #read0.transfer_count		bra exit@class1		ldy #read1.transfer_countexit		lda bytes_sent		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		lda bytes_sent+2		iny		iny		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		lda error		;there may be a non-fatal error here		cmp #$0001		;set carry to appropriate sign		rtserror		ds 1		ENDP		export check_access		;	check_access checks to see if the parameter block is specifying  ;	an invalid access for the open call.  The things that it checks;	for are: ;;		Are we trying to open the resource fork of a file.  ;		Are we trying to open the file other than read only.;;	If so it returns with the carry set and the accumulator set to the ;	appropriate error.  We do this here, instead of in the open_s routine;	because these are non_bouncing errors and we need to check this after;	we have determined that the target is a DOS file.check_access	PROCNAME						lda class		;get the class of the call		beq @done		;if class 0, no resource fork				lda  p_cnt		cmp #4			;enough parameters for request_access?		bcc @done		;no, can't check it				clc		ldy #open1.request_access		lda [param_blk_ptr],y	;get the request access word		and #%0000000000000010	;check for write access		beq @checkRez		;no write access				lda #invalid_access		bra @access_err@checkRez				lda  p_cnt		cmp  #5		bcc  @done		; pcount too small ->				clc		ldy  #open1.resource_number		lda  [<param_blk_ptr],y		beq  @done		; ok -> its not the resource fork				cmp #1			; == to 1		beq @fork_err		; can't open resource fork				lda #parm_range_err	; bad value for ressource_number		bra @access_err		@fork_err			lda  #res_not_found@access_err			sec@done				rts				ENDP						export openopen		PROCNAME		;handle the OPEN call		;brk $49		stz vcr_fcr_flags	;init flags		jsr open_setup		;init vars, set up buffers, put volume name in…					;…volname_buf_ptr, verify that volume is…					;…online, mount the volume		bcc @ok		brl err_exit		;deallocate stuff on the way out@ok;	we now have a valid vcr for the volume we want;	now see exactly what we're supposed to open				@process_file		;we now have a legal filename and a vcr		;now look for fcrs unless we just created the vcr		;brk $07		lda (file_name_ptr)	;was there a filename?		beq handle_vol		brl handle_filehandle_vol			;this section opens the volume "root" directory file				;first build string of vol name with leading colon				; but first check to see if for some reason the caller				;has specified the resource fork as the target or is trying				;to open this vol readWrite.				jsr check_access			bcc @h_vol	; nope! everythings OK here		brl err_exit	;deallocate stuff on the way out@h_vol		lda vol_name_buf		;get length		inc a			;account for colon character		sta scratch_str_buf		sep #$20		LONGA OFF		lda #':'		ldy #2		sta scratch_str_buf,y	;place the colon@loop		lda vol_name_buf,y		cmp #1			;save zero status in carry		iny			;position one byte over in dest string		sta scratch_str_buf,y		bcs @loop		;if character was non-zero, loop		rep #$20		LONGA ON		ldx #<scratch_str_buf		ldy #^scratch_str_buf		lda #fcr_size		jsl alloc_fcr		bcc @ok		brl err_exit		;can't get FCR@ok		jsl deref		stx fcr_ptr		sty fcr_ptr+2		lda #$4000		tsb vcr_fcr_flags	;set flag to say we allocated an FCR				;special fcr setup for root directory file		ldy #fcr_fst_id		lda #my_id		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #vcr_id		lda [vcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_vcr_id		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #vcr_buf_vp		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;the fcr has the same buffer as the vcr		tax		iny		iny		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;high word		ldy #fcr_buf_vp+2		sta [fcr_ptr],y		txa		dey		dey		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_mark		;zero the mark		lda #$0000		sta [fcr_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_eof+2		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;zero high word of eof		ldy #fcr_aux		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;zero aux_type		iny		iny		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_entry_num		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;zero the entry position for get_dir_entry				ldy #fcr_blks_used+2	;set blocks used		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;zero high word		dey		dey		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;low word of blocks used				xba			;transform to byte value for EOF		ldy #fcr_eof		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;that's our EOF!		ldy #fcr_type		lda #$000F		;GS/OS directory file		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_access		lda #access_unlocked		sta [fcr_ptr],ycount_dir			;count entries in the directory		stz dir_cnt		lda #$0000		;cat sector numbers start at 0@cat_loop		ldx #$0000		;same for fde's@fde_loop		sta cat_index		stx fde_index		;save these		jsr find_fde		bcc @ok		brl err_exit		;error@ok*** changed 6-May-93 DAL;;;		lda [fde_ptr]		;first byte tells whether in use;;;		and #$00FF		jsr load_fde_flag*** 6-May-93		beq @done		;a $00 means beyond last entry		cmp #$00FF		beq @inactive		;inactive, don't count it		inc dir_cnt@inactive		ldx fde_index		lda cat_index		inx			;next fde		cpx #$0007		;check limit of 7 fde's per cat sector		bcc @fde_loop		;we're ok, check next fde		ina			;next catalog sector		cmp cat_sec_count	;past our limit?		bcc @cat_loop		;move on to next cat sector@done		lda dir_cnt		ldy #fcr_tot_ent		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;save this for get_dir_entry		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		lda [vcr_ptr],y		inc a		bne @not_first		;if it was $FFFF, increment it again		inc a@not_first		sta [vcr_ptr],y		brl stuff_usr_prm_blkhandle_file		;brk $02;		ldy #vcr_open_cnt;		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;see if any files are already open in this vcr;		beq chk_dir		;if no open files, we'll have to look in the directory;;		inc a			;this field is inited to $FFFF;		beq chk_dir		;check for $FFFF also;;		jsr search_fcr		;this routine will return number of fcr for previous…;					;…open of the file in old_fcr (0 means none found);		bcc req_fcr		;we're ready to get a new fcr		chk_dir				;does this guy exist in the directory?		jsr check_dir		;this sub checks for filename in file_name_ptr		bcc @ok		lda #dir_error		;problem with the directory structure		brl err_exit@ok		lda fde_index		;if negative, we didn't find the file		bpl req_fcrfile_not_here			;file not on this volume		lda #file_not_found		brl err_exit		;now we have to allocate a new fcr		;but first lets check to see what fork the caller is trying to open	req_fcr		jsr check_access	;test for invalid operation		bcc @not_Rez		;if not resource fork		brl err_exit		;cleanup and return the appropriate error.@not_Rez		;first build string of vol name with leading colon		lda vol_name_buf	;get length		inc a			;account for colon character		sta scratch_str_buf		sep #$20		LONGA OFF		lda #':'		ldy #2		sta scratch_str_buf,y	;place the colon@loop		lda vol_name_buf,y		cmp #1			;save zero status in carry		iny			;position one byte over in dest string		sta scratch_str_buf,y		bcs @loop		;if character was non-zero, loop		rep #$20		LONGA ON		ldx #<scratch_str_buf	;alloc_fcr now gets volume name		ldy #^scratch_str_buf		lda #fcr_size		jsl alloc_fcr		bcc @ok1		lda #out_of_mem		;can't get an fcr		brl err_exit@ok1				;SCM has successfully allocated the FCR		jsl deref		stx <fcr_ptr		sty <fcr_ptr+2		lda #$4000		tsb vcr_fcr_flags	;set flag to say we allocated an FCR		lda #file_buf_size	;request segments for file buffers		jsl alloc_seg		bcc @ok2				;can't get needed buffers, cancel the OPEN		lda #out_of_mem		brl err_exit@ok2		tya			;stash the vp's in the fcr		ldy #fcr_buf_vp+2		sta [fcr_ptr],y		txa		dey		dey		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #vcr_open_cnt	;bump the open count in the vcr		lda [vcr_ptr],y		inc a		bne @not_first		;this field is inited to $FFFF		inc a@not_first		sta [vcr_ptr],yreset_mark		lda #$0000		ldy #fcr_mark		;offset to mark in fcr		sta [fcr_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;		lda old_fcr		;what was the result of the fcr dup search?;		beq fill_new_fcr	;first open for this file;		brl copy_fcr		;let's not reinvent this wheelfill_new_fcr		ldy #fcr_fde_num	;index to fde number of the file		lda fde_index		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_cat_sec	;sector where file's directory entry lives		lda cat_index		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_fst_id		;FST ID number		lda #my_id		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #vcr_id		;link to VCR		lda [vcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_vcr_id		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fde_type		;DOS 3.3 filetype		lda [fde_ptr],y		and #$007F		;mask high byte & lock bit		ldy #fcr_dos_type		sta [fcr_ptr],y		bra get_info		;now get info for param blockcopy_fcr		;copy appropriate stuff from old to new fcr		;brk $31		stz copy_fcr_ctr		ldy #0			;init index@big_loop		lda copy_fcr_ctr	;get counter of number of bitmapped words		lsr a		tax		lda copy_tbl,x		;get bitmapped word		sta copy_fcr_temp		ldx #16			;init counter@loop		asl copy_fcr_temp		bcc @no_copy		lda [old_fcr_ptr],y		sta [fcr_ptr],y@no_copy		iny		iny			;bump index by a word		dex			;decrement counter		bne @loop		;repeat for each bit		lda copy_fcr_ctr		bne @done		;if not 0, we're done (loop executes twice)		inc copy_fcr_ctr		bra @big_loop@done		bra stuff_usr_prm_blkget_info				;call get_file_info		;brk $01		ldy #fcr_buf_vp		;get the vp to the fcr's buffer		lda [fcr_ptr],y		tax		iny		iny		lda [fcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl deref		stx <drvr_buf_ptr		stx <fcr_buf_ptr		sty <drvr_buf_ptr+2		sty <fcr_buf_ptr+2					;hopefully, the device number will be left over from					;the "volume" routine		lda #drvr_read		sta <drvr_call_num		ldy #fcr_fde_num		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;need these to set up ptr to fde		tax		ldy #fcr_cat_sec		lda [fcr_ptr],y		jsr find_fde		;this sets up fde_ptr		jsr get_file_info	;get all the good stuff		bcc @ok1		brl err_exit@ok1				;now copy from globals to the fcr		ldy #fcr_data_sect		lda last_data_sec		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;make note of number of sector in buffer		ldy #fcr_access		lda access		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_eof		lda eof		sta [fcr_ptr],y		lda eof+2		iny		iny		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_aux		lda aux_type		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_type		lda os_type		sta [fcr_ptr],y		ldy #fcr_blks_used		lda blks_used		sta [fcr_ptr],y		lda #$0000		iny		iny		sta [fcr_ptr],y		;zero long word of blks_usedstuff_usr_prm_blk		;fill everything the user asked for		;brk $44		lda class		;get the class of the call		bne @class1		brl @class0@class1				lda p_cnt		tax			;keep countdown in x		ldy #$0000-2		;init Y for index to table in loop@cpy_loop		iny		iny			;move to next word entry		lda fcr_to_pblk,y	;get the table entry		asl a			;test 2 highest bits		bcc @no_dec		;should we decrement pcount?		dex		bmi @special		;if we hit bottom, go on to the special cases@no_dec		asl a			;test next bit		bcs @cpy_loop		;if original bit 14 was set, don't copy		lsr a		lsr a			;shift things back into place		phy			;save the present index		tay		lda [fcr_ptr],y		ply		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		bra @cpy_loop@special			;handle special case parameters		ldx p_cnt		cpx #8			;do we need aux_type?		bcc @done		ldy #open1.aux_type+2		lda #$0000		sta [param_blk_ptr],y	;zero the high word of aux_type		cpx #9			;need storage type?		bcc @done		ldy #fcr_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		cmp #$000F		;root directory?		beq @store_s_type	;filetype happens to equal storage type		lda #storage_type	;for regular files@store_s_type		ldy #open1.storage_type		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		cpx #10		bcc @done		lda #$0000		ldy #open1.create_date_time		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		cpx #11		bcc @done		ldy #open1.mod_date_time		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta [param_blk_ptr],y		cpx #12		bcc @done		ldy #open1.option_list		jsr do_option_list	;this routine needs offset in param blk in Y		bcc @done		lda #buff_too_small		bra err_exit@class0		ldy #fcr_ref_num		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get ref num from FCR		ldy #open0.ref_num		sta [param_blk_ptr],y	;set reference number@done;	Added zeroing of res eof;	-- Monte Benaresh 2/19/92 for 6.0.1		lda  p_cnt		; res eof included?		cmp  #$0E				bcc  @d1		; no ->				ldy  #open1.resource_eof		lda  #0		sta  [<param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta  [<param_blk_ptr],y		lda  p_cnt		; res blocks included?		cmp  #$0f				bcc  @d1		; no ->				ldy  #open1.resource_blocks		lda  #0		sta  [<param_blk_ptr],y		iny		iny		sta  [<param_blk_ptr],y@d1		clc		lda #$0000		rts			;all done with open!err_exit			;if an error occurs, return through here		;brk $91		pha			;save error code		bit vcr_fcr_flags	;that's the first time I've used this instruction!		php			;save result for VCR test below		bvc @no_fcr@cancel_fcr		ldy #fcr_type		lda [fcr_ptr],y		cmp #$000F		;is it a directory?		beq @not_dir		;if directory file then don't release its buffer…					;…because it is shared with the VCR		ldy #fcr_buf_vp		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get fcr buffer's vp so we can release it		tax		iny		iny		ora [fcr_ptr],y		;check for 0 vp		beq @invalid_vp		lda [fcr_ptr],y		tay		jsl release_seg@not_dir@invalid_vp		ldy #fcr_ref_num		lda [fcr_ptr],y		;get ref num		jsl release_fcr		;get rid of the FCR		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		lda [vcr_ptr],y		beq @open_cnt_ok	;if open count is 0, leave it alone		inc a			;check for $FFFF		beq @store_open_cnt	;change $FFFF to 0@dec_open_cnt		dec a			;reverse inc		dec a			;now decrement@store_open_cnt		sta [vcr_ptr],y		;Y reg should point to vcr_open_cnt@open_cnt_ok@no_fcr		plp			;restore result of bit instruction above		bpl @no_vcr		;high bit tells whether VCR was allocated@cancel_vcr		ldy #vcr_open_cnt		lda #$0000		sta [vcr_ptr],y		;must zero the open count to release it!		ldy #vcr_id		lda [vcr_ptr],y		;get ID of the VCR		jsl release_vcr		;this invokes sys_remove_vol call to this fst@no_vcr		pla			;restore error code		sec		rtscopy_tbl		;defines which words get copied into the new fcr for a multiply-opened			;file.  A 0 entry indicates that the word does NOT get copied.	;dc.w %0001100000100111;	      |;     first word in fcr;             last word in fcr;                     |	;dc.w %0011111100000000copy		equ $1no_copy		equ 0;	***** NOTE *****	The presence of comments after the line continuation	*****;				character (\) is NOT officially supported by the MAX;				assembler but works fine for version 1.1d9.;				If errors are generated for these lines by a later;				version of the assembler, remove all text between the;	****************	'\' and the carriage return.	|			*****;								|;								|;				bit position		field	|;				------------		-----	|	dc.w 0				++	\		•		no_copy		<< 0	++	\	fcr_ref_num		no_copy		<< 1	++	\	fcr_path_name		no_copy		<< 2	++	\	fcr_path_name (h)		copy		<< 3	++	\	fcr_fst_id		copy		<< 4	++	\	fcr_vcr_id (h)		no_copy		<< 5	++	\	fcr_level		no_copy		<< 6	++	\	fcr_newline		no_copy		<< 7	++	\	fcr_newline (h)		no_copy		<< 8	++	\	fcr_newline_len		no_copy		<< 9	++	\	fcr_mask		copy		<< 10	++	\	fcr_access		no_copy		<< 11	++	\	fcr_buf_vp		no_copy		<< 12	++	\	fcr_buf_vp (h)		copy		<< 13	++	\	fcr_eof		copy		<< 14	++	\	fcr_eof (h)		copy		<< 15		;	fcr_aux	dc.w 0				++	\		no_copy		<< 0	++	\	fcr_mark		no_copy		<< 1	++	\	fcr_mark (h)		copy		<< 2	++	\	fcr_type		copy		<< 3	++	\	fcr_dos_type		copy		<< 4	++	\	fcr_blks_used		copy		<< 5	++	\	fcr_blks_used (h)		copy		<< 6	++	\	fcr_cat_sec		copy		<< 7	++	\	fcr_fde_num		no_copy		<< 8		;	fcr_data_sec;	These words were derived from this table:;@copy		equ $1;@no_copy	equ 0;	dc.w @no_copy		;fcr_ref_num;	dc.l @no_copy		;fcr_path_name;	dc.w @copy		;fcr_fst_id;	dc.w @copy		;fcr_vcr_id;	dc.w @no_copy		;fcr_level;	dc.l @no_copy		;fcr_newline;	dc.w @no_copy		;fcr_newline_len;	dc.w @no_copy		;fcr_mask;	dc.w @copy		;fcr_access;		;fst-specific:;	dc.l @no_copy		;fcr_buf_vp;	dc.l @copy		;fcr_eof;	dc.w @copy		;fcr_aux;	dc.l @no_copy		;fcr_mark;	dc.w @copy		;fcr_type;	dc.w @copy		;fcr_dos_type;	dc.l @copy		;fcr_blks_used;	dc.w @copy		;fcr_cat_sec;	dc.w @copy		;fcr_fde_num;	dc.w @no_copy		;fcr_data_secfcr_to_pblk	;table to specify what data to copy from the fcr to the user		;parameter block.  each position corresponds to the same position		;in the user parameter block.		;each word entry contains:		;	bit 15 = decrement pcount--high for the 1st word in each parameter		;	bit 14 = copy inhibit--if high, nothing gets copied for this word position@no_copy	equ %0100000000000000@dec		equ %1000000000000000;		dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;pcount	dc.w @no_copy			;pcount <CAF> removed the @dec because pcount is not an actual parm.	dc.w fcr_ref_num	++ @dec	;ref_num	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;pathname (low)	dc.w @no_copy			;pathname (high)	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;request access	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;resource number	dc.w fcr_access		++ @dec	;access	dc.w fcr_type		++ @dec	;file_type	dc.w fcr_aux		++ @dec	;aux_type (low)	dc.w @no_copy			;aux_type (high)	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;storage_type	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;create_date_time (0)	dc.w @no_copy			;create_date_time (1)	dc.w @no_copy			;create_date_time (2)	dc.w @no_copy			;create_date_time (3)	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;mod_date_time (0)	dc.w @no_copy			;mod_date_time (1)	dc.w @no_copy			;mod_date_time (2)	dc.w @no_copy			;mod_date_time (3)	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;option_list (low)	dc.w @no_copy			;option_list (high)	dc.w fcr_eof		++ @dec	;eof (low)	dc.w fcr_eof+2			;eof (high)	dc.w fcr_blks_used	++ @dec	;blocks_used (low)	dc.w @no_copy+2			;blocks_used (high)	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;resource_eof (low)	;no entry			resource_eof (high)	dc.w @no_copy		++ @dec	;resource_blocks (low)	;no entry			resource_blocks (high)*** added 7-Nov-92 DAL to fix run-off-the-end-of-the-table problem	dc.w @no_copy++@dec*** end 7-Nov-92copy_fcr_temp	ds.w 1copy_fcr_ctr	ds.w 1;vcr_fcr_flags	ds.w 1		;bit 15 = VCR allocated during this call				;bit 14 = FCR allocated during this call				;these flags are read if an error occurs during the OPEN call…				;…so that any allocated structures may be released on abort		ENDP		END